ate Government/Union Territory \nAdministrations for Organizing Fair and Festivals and Tourism \nrelated Events. \n \n Ministry of Tourism promotes various tourism sites and \nproducts of different States/Union Territories including those in the \nStates of Madhya Pradesh and Chhattisgarh in the domestic and \ninternational markets through media campaigns and activities \nundertaken by Indiatourism domestic and overseas offices. \n \n Submission of project proposals by the State Governments/UT \nAdministrations under the above schemes is a continuous process. \nThe projects for development are identif ied in consultation with the \nState Governments/UT Administrations and are sanctioned subject \nto availability of funds, submission of suitable detailed project \nreports, adherence to scheme guidelines and utilization of funds \nreleased earlier. \n \n Details of p rojects sanctioned to the State Governments of \nMadhya Pradesh and Chhattisgarh under the above schemes during \nthe last three years and current year is given at Annexure. \n \n******** \n\nANNEXURE \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUE STION NO.†157  ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \nREGARDING DEVELOPMENT OF TOURIST PLACES IN MADHYA \nPRADESH AND CHHATTISGARH. \n \nSwadesh Darshan Scheme       (Rs. in Crore) \nSl. \nNo. \nState/UT Name of \nthe \nCircuit \nName of the \nProject \nAmt. \nSanctioned \nAmt. \nReleased \nYear 2015-16 \n1. Madhya \nPradesh \nWildlife \nCircuit \nDevelopment \nof Wildlife \nCircuit at \nPanna- \nMukundpur- \nSanjay- Dubri-\nBandhavgarh- \nKanha- Mukki- \nPench in \nMadhya \nPradesh. \n92.22 73.78 \n2. Chhattisgarh Tribal \nCircuit \nDevelopment \nof Tribal \nTourism \nCircuit in \nJashpur- \nKunkuri- \nMainpat- \nAmbikapur- \nMaheshpur -\nRatanpur- \nKurdar-\nSarodadadar- \nGangrel- \nKondagaon– \nNathiya \nNawagaon- \nJagdalpur- \nChitrakoot- \n99.21 73.29 \n\nTirthgarh in \nChhattisgarh.                                                             