rban Livelihoods  Mission  (NULM)  in  Se ptember \n2013  to  reduce  poverty  and vulnerability of urb an poor \nhouseholds by enabling them to access gainful self-employment \nand skilled wage employment opportunities, for impr ovement in \ntheir livelihoods on a sustainable basis. The missi on also aims \nto build strong grassroot level institutions of the  urban poor; \nprovide shelters equipped with essential services t o the urban \nhomeless and address livelihoods concerns of the urban street  \n...2/- \n \n\n-2- \n \nvendors by facilitating access to suitable spaces, institutional \ncredit, social security, etc. The Mission has been renamed as \nDeendayal Antyodaya Yojana - National Urban Livelih oods \nMission (DAY-NULM) and extended to all statutory to wns in the \ncountry since February, 2016. \nAs per the Mission Document, the Governing Council, which is a \npolicy making body at the national level, will lay down priorities \nand review overall progress and development of the Mission. \nFurther, the Executive Committee has also been cons tituted at \nnational level to oversee the activities of the Mis sion. In a \nsimilar way, the Mission Document prescribes for co nstitution, \nby the States/UTs, of their respective Governing Co uncils and \nthe Executive Committees. Meetings of these bodies are held \nfrom time to time to review the status of implement ation, \naddress the issues and bottlenecks, if any and prov ide \nnecessary direction to the Mission. State/UT- wise statement \non cumulative achievements, under various component s of \nDAY-NULM, is at Annexure-A.  \n***** \n\nAnnexure-A to the LSUQ No 426 for answer on 05.02.2019  \nCUMULATIVE PHYSICAL ACHIEVEMENTS UPTO 31.01.2019 UNDER DAY-NULM \nSl.  \nNo. \nNames of the \nStates/UTs \nNo. of Self -Help \nGroups (SHGs) \nformed \nNo. of SHGs for \ngiven \nRevolving Fund \n(RF) \nNo. of \nmembers \ntrained \nPlacement of \nSkill trained \nbeneficiaries \nNo. of beneficiaries \nassisted for setting \