li 0  0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n33 Daman & Diu 0  0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n34 Delhi 0  0 1095  0 0 0 190 0 \n35 Puducherry 40  2 0 0 11  12  1 0 \nTOTAL   357510  247168  1317399  476374"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |427", "t": "Fisheries Production in India", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY, DAIRYING AND FISHERIES \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 427 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 5TH FEBRUARY, 2019  \n \n \nFISHERIES PRODUCTION IN INDIA \n \n427. SHRI GUTHA SUKENDER REDDY: \n SHRI ANTO ANTONY:  \n          \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE  कृषि और ककसान कल्याण मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n \n \n(a) whether it is a fact that the Government has taken a decision to augment the fisheries \nproduction and provide sufficient infrastructure facilities for development of fisheries in the \ncountry and has recently constituted a new fund called “Fisheries Infrastructure Development \nFund” (FIDF) with Rs. 7,522 crore earmarked for the same, if so, the details thereof including \nthe salient features of the FIDF;  \n \n(b) whether the Government has any details regarding the number of proposals received \nfrom various S tates, and the number of propo sals approved as well as the fund allocated \nunder the FIDF so far and if so, the details thereof, State -wise, category -wise and amount -\nwise; and \n \n(c) the details thereof and the details o f the funds being provided to the State of \nTelangana for this purpose? \n \n \n \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \n                                                                                             (SHRIMATI KRISHNA RAJ) \n \n(a) to (c ) :  Yes, Madam.  The Union Government has re cently approved a proposal for \ncreation of Fisheries and Aquaculture Infrastructure Development Fund (FIDF ) with a total \nfund size of Rs. 7522.48 crore for creation of fisheries infrastructure facilities with a move to \naugment fish production in the Country. The FIDF provides concessional finance to the \nEligible Entities (EEs), including State Governments/UTs and State entities for development \nof identified fisheries infrastructure facilities . The conce ssional finance is provided by the \nNodal Loaning Entities (NLEs) namely (i) National Bank for Agriculture and Rural \nDevelopment (NABARD), (ii) National Cooperatives Development Corporation (NCDC)  \nand (iii) All scheduled Banks . Under the FIDF, the Governmen t of India provides interest \nsubvention up to 3% per annum  for providing the concessional finance by the NLEs at the \ninterest rate not lower than 5% per annum.  \n Details of the proposals submitted by various State Governments for financing under \nFIDF are f urnished at Annexure -I. As it is a new scheme, approval of project s under FIDF \nfor Eligible Entities (EEs) including State Governments/UTs and State entities is evaluated as \nper the operational guidelines of FIDF being finalized.  No proposal  has been received from \nthe Government of Telanagana . \n \n***** \n\nAnnexure-I \n \nStatement referred to in reply to the Lok Sabha Un starred Question No. 427 for answer \non 5th February, 2019 regarding Fisheries Production in India - Details of the proposals \nsubmitted by the Stat e Governments for setting up of new fishing harbours for \nfinancing under the Fisheries and Aquaculture Infrastructure Development Fund \n(FIDF) \n \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \nSl. \nNo.  \nName of the Fishing Harbour  District  Estimated cost \n(Rs. In lakhs) \nA Proposals of the Government of Tamil Nadu  \n1. Tharangampadi  Nagapattinam 12000.00 \n2. Vellapallam  Nagapattinam 10000.00 \n3. Thiruvottriyur Kuppam  Tiruvallur 20000.00 \n4. Development of existing Fishing Harbour at \nMudhunagar  \nCuddalore 10000.00 \n5. Construction of Groynes at Vallavila i, \nMarthandamthurai and Neerodi Village  \nKanniyakumari 11600.00 \n Total   63600.00 \nB Proposals of the Government of Andhra Pradesh \n1 Uppada East Godavari 28940.00 \n2 Vodarevu Prkasham 40922.00 \n3 Machilipattinam Krishna 25200.00 \n4 Nizampattinam Guntur 34078.00 \n Total  129140.00 "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |428", "t": "Safe City Project", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 428 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 05TH FEBRUARY, 2019/, MAGHA 16, 1940 (SAKA) \n \nSAFE CITY PROJECT \n \n428. SHRI B. VINOD KUMAR: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the success achieved so far by the  Ministry in implementing Safe City  \nProject; \n \n(b) the details of the share of  responsibility and budget between State  and \nCentre with regard to this project; and \n \n(c) the criteria likely to be adopted by  the Government  to select the next \nbatch of cities in the aforesaid project? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a): Empowered Committee of Officers for Nirbhaya funds scheme has \napproved pilot Safe  City projects in eight selected metropolitan cities, \nnamely, Delhi, Kolkata, Mumbai, Chennai, Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Ahmedabad \nand Lucknow with a view to provide safety to women in public places  at a \ntotal cost of Rs. 2919.55 crore. Out of these, funds hav e been released to \nStates for five projects. \n(b): The cost of the projects is shared between the Central Government and \nthe concerned States in 60:40 ratio. The Safe City Project in Delhi is fully \nfunded by the Central Government. \n(c): The criteria for selection of next batch of cities for the project have not \nbeen decided. \n***** \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |43", "t": "Quarterly Employment Survey", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 43 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \nQUARTERLY EMPLOYMENT SURVEY \n \n43. KUMARI SUSHMITA DEV: \n  \nWill the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate: \n  \n(a)whether it is a fact that the Government is no longer planning to \nrelease the Quarterly Employment Survey; and \n(b)if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI SANTOSH KUMAR GANGWAR) \n \n(a) & (b):  Ministry of Labour & Employment  had constituted a \ncommittee under the chairmanship of Prof. T.C.A . Anant, former \nSecretary, Ministry of Statistics & Programme Implementation, to \nexamine the relevance of Quarterly Employment Survey in the present \ncircumstances. The Committee has recently submitted its report to \nthe Government .  The report of the Committee is being examined in \nthe Ministry. \n \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |430", "t": "Involvement of Minors in Criminal Activities", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 430 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 05TH FEBRUARY, 2019/, MAGHA 16, 1940 (SAKA) \n \nINVOLVEMENT OF MINORS IN CRIMINAL ACTIVITIES \n \n430. SHRI LAXMI NARAYAN YADAV: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the number of minors involved in criminal activities is increasing \nin the country every year; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the reasons therefor; \n \n(c) the  number of crimes committed  by minors during the last three years, \nState-wise. \n \n(d) the efforts made by the  Government to check minors from  committing \nvarious crimes; and \n \n(e) the outcome thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a) to (c) : As per the latest published report of the National Crime Records \nBureau (NCRB), the number of cases registered against juveniles in the \ncountry during the years 2014, 2015 and 2016 are 38,455, 33,433 and 35,849 \nrespectively, which shows a mixed trend. State/UT wise details are given in \nAnnexure. \n(d) & (e) :  ‘Police’ and ‘Public Order’ are State subjects under the Seventh \nSchedule to the Constitution of India and therefore, the responsibility to \nmaintain law and or der rests with the respective State Governments. The \nissue of  crime by juveniles is mainly  dealt with through the Juvenile  Justice \n-2/… \n\n-2- \nLS.USQ.NO.430 FOR 05.02.2019 \n(Care and Protection of Children) Act, 2015 which provides for reformative \ncare in case of children/juveniles in conflict with law. The Ministry of Women \nand Child Development is implementing a Centrally Sponsored Scheme, \nnamely, Integrated Child Protection Scheme (ICPS) for rehabilitation and \nreintegration of children in difficult circu mstances including children in \nconflict with law. Under the scheme, there is a provision of Counselor in \nObservation Homes to provide counseling services to children in conflict with \nlaw and in need of care and protection as well as for their parents and \nfamilies. The Act and the Central Juvenile Justice (Care and Protection \nof Children) Model Rules, 2016 provide for setting up of a network of services \nand structures for ensuring the well being and rehabilitation of such children, \nwhich include Juvenile Jus tice Boards, Special Juvenile Police Units, State \nand District Child Protection Units, Homes of various types and non -\ninstitutional care through adoption, foster -care and sponsorship. These \nmeasures inter alia  also intend main -streaming of children in conf lict with \nlaw. The State Governments/UT Administrations are entrusted with the \nprimary responsibility for implementation of the provisions of Juvenile \nJustice (Care and Protection of Children) Act, 2015.  \n***** \n  \n\n                 \nAnnexure \nState/UT-wise Cases Registered against juveniles (CR), Juneviles Apprehended (JUVAPP) Under Juveniles in Conflict with Law during 2014-2016 \nSL State/UT \n2014 2015 2016 \nTotal Cognizable \nIPC Crimes \nTotal Cognizable \nSLL Crimes Total Total Cognizable \nIPC Crimes \nTotal Cognizable \nSLL Crimes Total Total Cognizable \nIPC Crimes \nTotal Cognizable \nSLL Crimes Total \nCR JUVAPP CR JUVAPP CR JUVAPP CR TOTJUV CR TOTJUV CR JUVAPP CR TOTJUV CR TOTJUV CR JUVAPP \n1 Andhra Pradesh 871 1002 12 16 883 1018 1002 1350 13 21 1015 1371 802 1215 7 14 809 1229 \n2 \nArunachal \nPradesh 77 120 4 6 81 126 62 145 4 11 66 156 56 78 1 2 57 80 \n3 Assam 466 531 21 22 487 553 580 685 44 49 624 734 403 446 33 34 436 480 \n4 Bihar 4044 5800 327 604 4371 6404 1562 1573 96 101 1658 1674 2169 2443 166 183 2335 2626 \n5 Chhattisgarh 1611 1916 80 90 1691 2006 1788 2111 126 179 1914 2290 1834 2262 119 132 1953 2394 \n6 Goa 63 110 1 3 64 113 27 34 1 1 28 35 21 26 0 0 21 26 \n7 Gujarat 1595 1840 2785 2807 4380 4647 1356 1733 221 224 1577 1957 1561 1954 120 131 1681 2085 \n8 Haryana 994 1123 47 58 1041 1181 1012 1238 86 95 1098 1333 1051 1218 135 140 1186 1358 \n9 Himachal Pradesh 262 328 10 14 272 342 186 228 9 13 195 241 194 251 10 12 204 263 \n10 Jammu & Kashmir 100 137 2 2 102 139 176 244 5 5 181 249 188 309 10 10 198 319 \n11 Jharkhand 145 164 5 9 150 173 112 112 12 12 124 124 126 124 14 18 140 142 \n12 Karnataka 376 607 36 33 412 640 398 636 48 56 446 692 436 601 17 26 453 627 \n13 Kerala 1069 1432 134 143 1203 1575 1177 1570 221 223 1398 1793 553 967 75 93 628 1060 \n14 Madhya Pradesh 6346 7607 166 195 6512 7802 6320 7586 263 284 6583 7870 7219 8303 150 161 7369 8464 \n15 Maharashtra 5175 6947 232 281 5407 7228 5482 7123 211 247 5693 7370 6239 7400 367 312 6606 7712 \n16 Manipur 20 32 3 4 23 36 13 21 4 4 17 25 6 8 4 4 10 12 \n17 Meghalaya 120 161 5 8 125 169 96 125 15 16 111 141 70 79 14 14 84 93 \n18 Mizoram 44 52 0 0 44 52 34 44 7 7 41 51 49 59 4 4 53 63 \n19 Nagaland 9 9 1 1 10 10 14 30 3 3 17 33 16 23 2 2 18 25 \n20 Odisha 813 1040 25 37 838 1077 910 1069 24 26 934 1095 977 1265 17 20 994 1285 \n21 Punjab 253 332 24 26 277 358 102 138 9 10 111 148 103 141 14 16 117 157 \n22 Rajas"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |432", "t": "PM Krishi Sinchayee Yojana", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n432\n                     \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE  \n5\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY\n, 201\n9\n \n \nPM KRISHI SINCHAYEE YOJANA\n \n \n432. \n \nSHRI JANARDAN SINGH SIGRIWAL: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government has launched Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana\n \n(PMKSY) for the benefit of farmers in various States of the country; \n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details and objectives thereof; \n \n \n(c) \n \nthe details of the facilities being provided by the Government under the said Yojana to \nBihar; \n \n \n(d) \n \nwhether the Government has \nreviewed the overall implementation of the Yojana and if \nso, the results achieved so far under the Yojana, State/UT\n-\nwise including Bihar; and \n \n \n(e) \n \nthe other steps being taken by the Government to ensure that water reaches every \nfarm in the country?\n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF  STATE IN THE  MINISTRY OF  AGRICULTURE AND  FARMERS  WELFARE\n \n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \nमं\u0000ालय म\u0000 रा\u0000य \nमं\u0000ी\n  \n   \n       \n( SHRI PARSHOTTAM RUPALA)\n  \n \n \n(a) to (c)\n:\n \n \nPradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana\n \n(PMKSY) was launched during the \nyear 2015\n-\n16 with the objective to enhance physical access of water and expand cultivable \narea under assured irrigation, improve on\n-\nfarm water use efficiency, introduce sustainable \nwater conservation practices, etc. The com\nponents of PMKSY and the facilities/ activities \nbeing provided to States including Bihar under each of the component is as under: \n \n \nProgramme Components: \n \ni\n.\n \n   \nAccelerated Irrigation Benefit Programme(AIBP): \nTo focus on faster completion of \nongoing Major and\n \nMedium Irrigation projects including National Projects.  This \ncomponent is being implemented by Ministry of Water Resources, RD&GR\n.\n \n \n \nii\n.\n \n   \nPMKSY \n-\nHar Khet Ko Pani: \nSource augmentation, distribution, ground water \ndevelopment, lift irrigation, diversion of wa\nter from water plenty to water scarce areas, \nrepair, restoration, renovation of traditional water bodies. \n \nThis component is being \nimplemented by Ministry of Water Resources, RD&GR. \n \n \nContd….2/\n-\n \n\n \n-\n2\n-\n \n \niii\n.\n \n \nPMKSY\n-\n \nPer Drop More Crop:\n \nMicro\n-\nirrigation systems viz. Drip & Sprinkler irrigation \nsystems, Micro level storage structures, secondary storage, efficient water conveyance, \nwater lifting devices etc.\n  \nThis component is being implemented by Department of \nAgriculture, Cooperation and\n \nFarmers Welfare. \n \n \niv\n.\n \nPMKSY\n-\n \nWatershed Development Component:\n \nRidge area treatment, drainage line \ntreatment, soil and moisture conservation, water harvesting structure, livelihood support \nactivities and other watershed works. \nThis component is being implemen\nted by \nDepartment of Land Resources. \n \n \n(d)\n:\n \nThe progress of implementation of Yojana is being reviewed/ monitored regularly at \ndifferent levels. The State wise  achievements of various components of Yojana including \nBihar is given at Annexure\n-\nI to III:\n \n \n(e)\n:     \n \nThe following steps are taken under PMKSY to ensure that water reaches every farm \nin the country:\n \n \ni\n.\n \nCreation of new water sources; repair, restoration of defunct water sources; \nconstructions of water harvesting structures for secondary & micro sto\nrage etc.\n \n \nii\n.\n \nDeveloping/augmenting distribution network where irrigation sources (both assured \nand protective) are available or created\n.\n \n \niii\n.\n \nPromoting efficient water conveyance and field application devices within the farm viz, \nunderground piping system, Drip \n& Sprinklers, pivots, rain\n-\nguns and other application \ndevices etc\n.\n \n \niv\n.\n \nEncouraging community irrigation through registered user groups/ Farmer Producer \nOrganisations and\n \n \nv\n.\n \nFarmer oriented activities like capacity building, training and exposure visits, etc.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nI \n \n \n \nLok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 432 for 05.02.2019\n \n \nState wise details of projects completed/almost complete under PMKSY\n-\nAIBP\n \n \n \nSI. No\n \nState\n \nCompleted/almost complete projects\n \n1\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n1\n \n2\n \nChhattisgarh\n \n2\n \n3\n \nJammu & \nKashmir\n \n1\n \n4\n \nKarnataka\n \n2\n \n5\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \n10\n \n6\n \nMaharashtra\n \n5\n \n7\n \nOdisha\n \n2\n \n8\n \nPunjab\n \n2\n \n9\n \nRajasthan\n \n2\n \n10\n \nTelangana\n \n3\n \n11\n \nUttar Pradesh\n \n1\n \n                          \nTotal\n \n31\n \n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nII \n \n \nLok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 432 for 05.02.2019\n \n \n \nArea of coverage under Micro Irrigation under PMKSY\n-\nPer Drop More Crop, in Ha \n \n \nS.No.\n \nState\n \n2015\n-\n16\n \n2016\n-\n17\n \n2017\n-\n18\n \n2018\n-\n19\n \n(As on \n30.01.2019)\n \n1\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n94104\n \n141098\n \n186441\n \n149854\n \n2\n \nBihar\n \n5155\n \n4228\n \n3143\n \n0\n \n3\n \nChhattisgarh\n \n8056\n \n19227\n \n13087\n \n15218\n \n4\n \nGoa\n \n92\n \n123\n \n236\n \n0\n \n5\n \nGujarat\n \n142681\n \n165948\n \n143"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |433", "t": "Procurement of Foodgrains", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 433   \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 05 FEBRUARY, 2019 \n \nPROCUREMENT OF FOODGRAINS \n \n433.  SHRI RAJU SHETTY:  \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC \nDISTRIBUTION miHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h   be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether food items like wheat, arhar were procured to give relief to \nthe farmers when market rate were fallen t o assure Minimum Support Price \nduring last three four years;  \n \n(b)  if so, the details of the quantum of these food items purchased from \nfarmers, State-wise;  \n \n(c)  whether any irregularity was noticed during purchase, transport and \nstorage of these commodities;  \n \n(d)  whether the storage capacity for surplus grains area available in the \ncountry and if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(e)  if not, the manner in which the Gover nment will tackle such situation \nin future? \nA N S W E R \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR  CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI C. R. CHAUDHARY) \n(a) & (b):  Details of wheat and Arhar (Tur) procured by Government \nagencies at Minimum Support Price from farmers during last three year and \ncurrent year are at Annexure-I and II respectively. \n \n(c):  Immediate action is taken by the State Governments or Food \nCorporation of India (FCI), as the case may be, if any instance of irregularity \nis noticed or reported. \n \n(d) & (e):  The overall storage capacity required for central pool \nfoodgrains in the country is about 650 Lakh Metric Tonnes (LMT). Against \nthis, the total storage capacity available with Food Corporation of India (FCI), \nCentral Warehousing Corporation (CWC) and State Agencies (both owned and \nhired capacity), is 851.54 LMT (as on 31.12.2018) comprising 724.79 LMT in \ncovered godowns and 126.75 LMT in Cover and Plinth (CAP) storage. \n \nBesides, Government is implementing Private Entrepreneurship \nGuarantee (PE G) Scheme and has taken up construction of godowns and \nSteel Silos. \n****  \n \n\nANNEXURE-I \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) & (b) OF THE UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 433  DUE FOR ANSWER ON 5 TH FEBRUARY, 2019 IN THE LOK \nSABHA \n \n  \n   \n \n  \n     