sewerage collection and treatment \nand drainage systems;  \n  \n(c) if so, the details thereof;  \n  \n(d) whether under it Country’s first solar-powered sewage treatment plant will be installed; \nand  \n  \n(e) if so, the details thereof along with location selected for the plant?  \n  \n  \nANSWER  \nMINISTER OF STATE FORMINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION  \n(SHRI RAMESH CHANDAPPA JIGAJINAGI)  \n  \n  \n(a) to (e) Yes, Madam. The Loan Agreement for the Tranche-I of Tamil Nadu Urban Flagship \nInvestment Program for US $169 million was executed  between Asian Development Bank \nand Government of India on 16.11.2018. The proposed  Sewerage Treatment Plant in \nCoimbatore under Ground Sewage sub-project is going  to be powered  by a solar power \nplant. In addition, all the sewage pumping stations  are proposed with energy efficient pump \nsets and odour control devices. Solar Power Plant o f the capacity of 2 MW is proposed in \nCoimbatore city for operation of the Sewerage Treatment Plant.  \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |733", "t": "Load Carrying Capacity of Heavy Vehicles", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 733 \nANSWERED ON 7TH FEBRUARY, 2019 \n \nLOAD CARRYING CAPACITY OF HEAVY VEHICLES \n \n733.  DR. P. VENUGOPAL: \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  \n \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the load carrying capacities of heavy vehicles, including trucks, have been increased by \n20 to 25 per cent at par with global standards;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether it would help in reducing logistic costs; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a) & (b) Yes, Madam. The load carrying capacities of rig id vehicles has be en increased vide  \nthis Ministry’s NotificationsS.O. 3467(E) dated 16.07.2018 and S.O. 3881(E) dated 06.08.2018. \n \n(c)& (d)  With the advancement and improvements in truck manufacturing technology, and the \nNational Highways (NHs) designed to carry and support much heavier loads, the Ministry has \nconsidered for enhancing G ross Vehicle Weight (G VW) norms which may not only lead to better \ncompliance of the load limits by the truckers but also help in reducing the overall logistics co sts in \nthe country. \n \n***** \n \n \n  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |734", "t": "Road Connectivity in Rajasthan", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 734 \nANSWERED ON 07TH FEBRUARY, 2019 \n \nROAD CONNECTIVITY IN RAJASTHAN \n \n734. SHRI SUKHBIR SINGH JAUNAPURIA:  \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether all the villages and Dhanis  of Rajasthan have been connected with  approach \nroads, if so, the details thereof; \n(b) if not, the number of villages and Dhanis yet to be connected with approach roads and the \ntime by which this work is likely to be completed, if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether any remedial measures  have been adopted by the Government to  ensure the \nmonitoring of specific requirements during the construction of roads in the villages; and \n(d) if so, the details in respect of Tonk and Sawai Madhopur district? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY \n OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n \n \n(a) and (b) Out of total 16,726 identified eligible unconnected habitations, 16,038 have been \ncleared and 15,957 habitations have already been connected.   \n \n(c) and (d) The Ministry of Rural Development, in order to bring more transparency and \nefficiency to facil itate the implementation of the flagship Programme under Pradhan Mantri \nGram SadakYojona (PMGSY) Scheme, has adopted a web based online monitoring system \nfor all the PMGSY projects including Tonk and Sawai Madhopur districts in integration of \nOnline Manage ment Monitoring and Accounting System (OMMAS) with a Generic e -\nProcurement System (GePNIC). \n \n*** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |735", "t": "Study on Recent Floods", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES,\nRIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 735\nANSWERED ON 07.02.2019\nSTUDY ON RECENT FLOODS\n735. ADV. JOICE GEORGE\nWill the Minister of WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA\nREJUVENATION be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Union Government has studied or constituted an expert panel to study the recent\nflood induced aquatic changes in the State of Kerala;\n(b) if so, the details thereof;\n(c) whether the Union Government has received any requests in this regard from the State\nGovernment and the public;\n(d) if so, the details thereof; and\n(e) whether the Union Government has noted the issue with due importance and if so, the details\nthereof along with the steps taken to improve the situation?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND\nGANGA REJUVENATION & PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS\n(SHRI ARJUN RAM MEGHWAL)\n(a) & (b) After the recent floods of August, 2018, a study on the hydrological processes of the\nflood has been carried out by Central Water Commission (CWC). As per the study, Kerala\nexperienced an abnormally high rainfall from 1 June, 2018 to 19 August, 2018. As per Ind ian\nMeteorological Department (IMD) data, Kerala received 2346.6 mm of rainfall from 1 June,\n2018 to 19 August, 2018 in contrast to an expected 1649.5 mm of rainfall. This rainfall was\nabout 42% above the normal. Further, the rainfall over Kerala during 1s t to 19 th of August was\n164% above normal. Due to heavy rainfall, the first onset of flooding occurred towards the end\nof July. A severe spell of rainfall was experienced at several places on the 8 th and 9th of August,\n2018. Another severe spell of rainfal l started from the 14 th of August and continued till the 19 th\nof August, resulting in disastrous flooding in 13 out of 14 districts.\nAs informed by State Government of Kerala, the preliminary observation after the heavy\nfloods is that the water level in some rivers have receded drastically, and sediments/ sands were\ndeposited in the river itself and caused hindrance to the smooth flow in the river.\nContd…P/2\n\n//2//\nThe preliminary assessment conducted by the Irrigation Department, Government of\nKerala reveals that the topography of the land adjacent to rivers which were overflowing in the\nflood lost its topsoil and in some areas, the adjacent lands were totally washe d away and river\nitself took a new course. As informed by State Government of Kerala, Haritha Keralam Mission\nin association with Kerala State Remote Sensing Agency has initiated a study on the\nmorphological changes of the river bed.\n(c) to (e) In order t o explore the feasibility of development of flood forecasting/ early warning\nsystem and operation rules for reservoir operation, Ministry of Water Resources, River\nDevelopment & Ganga Rejuvenation in August, 2018, constituted a Joint Team comprising of\nofficials of Central Water Commission (CWC) and National Project Monitoring Unit (NPMU)\nof National Hydrology Project (NHP) with Chief Engineer, Cauvery and Southern Rivers\nOrganisation, CWC, Coimbatore as Team Leader. The Joint Team visited Kerala during 24 th to\n27th September, 2018, had discussions with Kerala Government authorities and assessed the\nsituation. After field visit and discussion, the relevant issues identified were studied in detail\nand the final report of the Committee was submitted to Governm ent of Kerala in December,\n2018 along with recommendations. During the interaction of the Joint Team and field visit in\nKerala, Government of Kerala requested to explore the possibility of establishing flood\nforecasting stations in Kerala after the study. Accordingly, the team decided to study\nimplementing of flood forecasting stations, initially in the three basins of Kerala i.e. (i) Pamba\n(ii) Periyar and (iii) Bharathapuzha.\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |736", "t": "Community Toilets in AP", "head": "Government of India \nMinistry of Drinking Water and Sanitation \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 736  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07-02-2019 \nCommunity Toilets in AP \n736. SHRI J.C. DIVAKARREDDY \nWill the Minister of  DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION be pleased to state : \n(a) whether the Government of Andhra Pradesh is foc using on construction of community \ntoilets in select villages of Vizianagaram, Anantap ur and Srikakulam districts as many \npeople are unable to construct toilets at their houses due to space constraints, if so, the details \nthereof and the financial assistance being provided  to AP State by Union Government since \nthe inception of the scheme, year and district-wise in the State;  \n(b) the details of the construction of individual a nd community toilets in select villages as \npart of the steps to achieve 100% ‘Open Defecation Free’ (ODF) status for the districts by \nFebruary, 2018 in AP State;  \n(c) whether the construction of individual toilets had been going on smoothly in tribal areas \ntoo in Andhra Pradesh including Araku, Paderu and o ther areas, if so, the details thereof and \nif not, the reasons therefor; and  \n(d) the funds sanctioned/spent for the ODF in triba l areas since inception of the scheme in \nAP State? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE  \nMINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION \n(SHRI RAMESH CHANDAPPA JIGAJINAGI) \n \n(a)&(b) As per the information received from the Go vernment of Andhra Pradesh, \nCommunity Sanitary Complexes (CSCs) have been sanct ioned in Vizianagaram, \nAnanthapurand Srikakulam districts based on the requirement and proposals submitted bythe \ndistricts.The State has already becomeOpen Defecati on Free (ODF) on 07.07.2018.  The \ndetails of individual household latrines (IHHLs) an d CSCs constructed in Vizianagaram, \nAnanthapurand Srikakulam districts are as given below: \n \nSl. \nNo. \n \nDistrict  No. of IHHLs \nconstructed  \nNo. of CSCs \nconstructed  \n1. Vizianagaram  3,23,910  496  \n2. Ananthapur 2,80,887 2603 \n3.  Srikakulam  3,43 ,565  3725  \n \nAs sanitation is a State subject, Swachh Bharat Mis sion (Gramin) [SBM(G)] is being \nimplemented through State/UT Governments.  Hence, t he funds under the programme are \nreleased to the States.  Further allocation/release  of the same to the districts is the \n\nresponsibility of the States.The details of funds r eleased by the Government of India to \nAndhra Pradesh since 2014-15 are given below: \n \n \nSl.No. Financial Year Amount released \n(Rs. in crore) \n1 2014-15 116.10 \n2 2015-16 234.17 \n3 2016-17 342.21 \n4 2017 -18  1190.71  \n5 2018-19 (up to 05.02.2019) 690.58 \nTotal  2573.77  \n \n(c)& (d)Yes, Madam.The details of IHHLs constructed and funds spent for the ODF in tribal \nareas in Andhra Pradesh sinceinception of the schem e, as per the information received from \nthe State Government,aregiven below:- \n \nSl. \nNo. \nIntegrated Tribal \nDevelopment Agency \n(ITDA) \nNo. of IHHLs \nconstructed \nFunds spent \n(Rs. in lakh) \n1 Srisailam  28223  5080.14  \n2 Rampachodavaram 18475 3325.5 \n3 Chintoor 9796 1763.28 \n4 Seethapeta 42901 7722.18 \n5 Parvathipuram 73285 13191.30 \n6 Paderu  52836  9510.48  \nTotal 2,25,516 40,592.88 \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |737", "t": "Conversion of Public Vehicles into e-Vehicles", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 737 \nANSWERED ON 07TH FEBRUARY, 2019 \n \n                       CONVERSION OF PUBLIC VEHICLES INTO E-VEHICLES  \n \n737. SHRIMATI RANJANBEN BHATT: \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  \n \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to convert public vehicles running on petrol and diesel into \nelectric vehicles; \n(b) if so, whether the Government has taken any step in this regard so far; and \n(c) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a) to (c)  The Government had notified GSR 629(E) dated 24 th June, 2016 for retro -fitment of \nhybrid electric system or electric kit to vehicles  running on petrol  and diesel and S.O. 1013(E) \ndated 15th April, 2015 specifying the type approval procedure of electric hybrid vehicles.   \n******* "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |738", "t": "FM Radio Stations", "head": "        \n   \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n MINISTRY OF INFORMATION & BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 738 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019) \n \nFM RADIO STATIONS \n738.  SHRI BALABHADRA MAJHI: \n \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING be pleased to state:  \n(a)  the details of FM radio stations that have been made operational during the \nlast four years, State-wise;  \n(b)  whether FM radio stations proposed in Nabarangpur and Malkangiri districts \nof Odisha are made operational and if so, the details thereof; and  \n(c)  if not, the time by which these are likely to be operational? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF \nINFORMATION AND BROADCASTING  \n{COL RAJYAVARDHAN RATHORE (Retd.)} \n  \n(a)     Prasar Bharati has informed that 90 FM stations have been made operational \nduring last four years and current year. State-wise details are given at Annexure-I.  \nAs regards Private FM Radio Channels, 13 7 new private FM radio channels \nhave been operationalized in the country  during last four years and current year.  \nState wise details are given at Annexure-II.  \n(b) & (c) All India Radio  has approved  plan of setting up 100 W FM relay radio \nstation at 100 locations including that in Nabarangpur and Malkangiri  districts of \nOdisha.  \n\n \n \nAnnexure-I \nANNEXURE AS REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PAR T (a) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 738 FOR ANSWER ON 07.02.2019 \n \nDetails of FM Radio Stations made operational during last four Years and \ncurrent year \nS.NO. STATE  2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 \n1 ANDHRA PRADESH 1 0 0 0 0 \n2 ARUNACHAL \nPRADESH 13 0 0 1 0 \n3 ASSAM 5 0 0 2 1 \n4 BIHAR 0 0 0 1 0 \n5 CHHATTISGARH 0 0 1 0 0 \n6 GOA 0 0 0 0 0 \n7 GUJARAT 0 0 1 0 0 \n8 HARYANA 0 0 0 0 0 \n9 HIMACHAL PRADESH 0 0 0 0 0 \n10 JAMMU & KASHMIR 0 0 0 0 2 \n11 JHARKHAND 0 0 0 0 0 \n12 KARNATAKA 1 0 0 0 0 \n13 KERALA 1 0 0 0 0 \n14 MADHYA PRADESH 0 0 1 0 1 \n15 MAHARASHTRA 1 2 1 0 1 \n16 MANIPUR 0 0 0 1 0 \n17 MEGHALAYA 1 0 0 2 0 \n18 MIZORAM 3 0 0 0 0 \n19 NAGALAND 2 0 0 2 0 \n20 ODISHA 3 1 1 0 0 \n21 PUNJAB 0 1 0 0 1 \n22 RAJASTHAN 0 0 0 2 2 \n23 SIKKIM 9 0 0 0 0 \n24 TAMIL NADU 1 0 0 0 0 \n25 TELANGANA 0 1 0 0 0 \n\n26 TRIPURA 6 0 0 2 0 \n27 UTTAR PRADESH 1 0 0 0 2 \n28 UTTARAKHAND 0 3 0 1 0 \n29 WEST BENGAL 0 0 3 1 1 \n30 ANDAMAN & \nNICOBAR (UT) 0 0 0 0 0 \n31 CHANDIGARH (UT) 0 0 0 0 0 \n32 DADAR & NAGAR \nHAVELI (UT) 0 0 0 0 0 \n33 DAMAN & DIU (UT) 0 0 0 0 0 \n34 DELHI (UT) 0 0 0 0 0 \n35 LAKSHADWEEP (UT) 0 0 0 0 0 \n36 PUDUCHERRY (UT) 0 0 0 0 0 \nTotal  48 8 8 15 11 \n \n  \n\n \nAnnexure -II \nANNEXURE AS REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PAR T (a) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 738 FOR ANSWER ON 07.02.2019 \n \nDetails of Private FM Radio Channels made operational during last four Years \nand current year \n \nS.NO. STATE  2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 \n1 ANDHRA PRADESH 0 0 0 0 5 \n2 ARUNACHAL \nPRADESH 0 0 0 1 0 \n3 ASSAM 0 1 0 0 1 \n4 BIHAR 0 0 2 3 1 \n5 CHHATTISGARH 0 0 1 2 0 \n6 GOA 0 0 0 0 0 \n7 GUJARAT 0 0 4 0 12 \n8 HARYANA 0 0 2 0 0 \n9 HIMACHAL PRADESH 0 0 0 0 0 \n10 JAMMU & KASHMIR 0 0 0 3 3 \n11 JHARKHAND 0 0 1 0 0 \n12 KARNATAKA 0 0 1 0 2 \n13 KERALA 0 0 1 2 0 \n14 MADHYA PRADESH 0 0 0 0 0 \n15 MAHARASHTRA 0 0 17 6 4 \n16 MANIPUR 0 0 0 0 0 \n17 MEGHALAYA 0 0 1 1 0 \n18 MIZORAM 0 0 0 2 0 \n19 NAGALAND 0 0 0 0 0 \n20 ODISHA 0 0 0 3 0 \n21 PUNJAB 0 0 2 0 0 \n22 RAJASTHAN 0 0 9 0 0 \n23 SIKKIM 0 0 0 0 0 \n24 TAMIL NADU 0 0 1 8 0 \n25 TELANGANA 0 0 3 0 3 \n\n26 TRIPURA 0 0 0 1 0 \n27 UTTAR PRADESH 0 0 11 9 2 \n28 UTTARAKHAND 0 0 0 0 1 \n29 WEST BENGAL 0 0 0 0 1 \n30 ANDAMAN & \nNICOBAR (UT) 0 0 0 0 0 \n31 CHANDIGARH (UT) 0 0 2 0 0 \n32 DADAR & NAGAR \nHAVELI (UT) 0 0 0 0 0 \n33 DAMAN & DIU (UT) 0 0 0 0 0 \n34 DELHI (UT) 0 1 0 0 0 \n35 LAKSHADWEEP (UT) 0 0 0 0 0 \n36 PUDUCHERRY (UT) 0 0 0 0 1 \nTotal  0 2 58 41 36 \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |739", "t": "Inspection of Silt in Ganga River", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES,\nRIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †739\nANSWERED ON 07.02.2019\nINSPECTION OF SILT IN GANGA RIVER\n†739. SHRI KAUSHALENDRA KUMAR\nWill the Minister of WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA\nREJUVENATION be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Union Government has conducted any inspection of the silt deposited in Ganga river\nparticularly in Bihar and if so, the details thereof;\n(b) whether the Union Government has received any report of the same and if so, the details thereof;\n(c) whether the State Government has also been included in the work of inspection; and\n(d) if so, the details thereof?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA\nREJUVENATION & PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS\n(SHRI ARJUN RAM MEGHWAL)\n(a) & (b) On the request of State Government of Bihar regarding the issue of floods and siltation in the\nState, a Central team led by Secretary, Ministry of Water Resources, River Development & Ganga\nRejuvenation, along with senior officials and experts viz. Shri A.B. Pandya, former Chairman, Central\nWater Commission and Prof. Z. Ahmed, IIT Roorkee, had visited the State on 5 th June, 2017 and held\ndiscussions with State Government officials. An aerial survey of the reach of river Ganga from Buxar to\nFarakka was carried out by this team.\nThe Central team held discussions with Hon’ble Chief Minister of Bihar along with State\nGovernment officials and experts. Subsequently, a Committee was constituted under the Chairmanship\nof Shri A.B. Pandya, Former Chairman, Central Water Commission (CWC), to address the issues of\nfloods and siltation in the State of Bihar. The opinion of State Government of Bihar was also obtained in\nrespect of constitution of this Committee including its Terms of Reference. The Committee has since\nsubmitted its report to the Ministry of Water Resources, River Development and Ganga Rejuvenation\nwhich has been circulated for wider consultation.\n(c) & (d) The Committee during one of its meeting, conducted an aerial survey of reaches of river\nGanga from Buxar to Farakka and reach of river Ghaghra from Ganga -Ghagra confluence to Turtipar.\nThe officials of Water Resources Department, Government of Bihar and Water and Land Management\nInstitute, Patna also participated in this aerial survey, apart from other members of the Committee.\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |74", "t": "Promotion of Tourism in Kerala", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.74 \nANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \nPROMOTION OF TOURISM IN KERALA \n \n74.  SHRI N.K. PREMACHANDRAN:  \nSHRI MULLAPPALLY RAMACHANDRAN:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Government has received any proposals for the \ndevelopment and promotion of tourism in the State of Kerala \nand if so, the details thereof along with the status of such \nproposals;  \n(b)  whether the Government has sanctioned any projects for the \nMalabar region of the State and if so, the details thereof;  \n(c)  the details of growth of tourism sector in the country during \nthe last four years along with the funds sanctioned for various \ntourism projects, State-wise including Kerala;  \n(d)  whether the Gov ernment has taken note of the advisory/alert \nissued by some countries to their citizens regarding their visit \nto India especially Kerala and if so, the details thereof and the \nreasons therefor along with the reaction of the Government \nthereto; and  \n(e)  whether the Government has initiated action to make a tourist \nfriendly climate in Kerala and if so, the details thereof along \nwith the initiatives taken by the Government to promote \ntourism in Kerala? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n(SHRI K.J. ALPHONS) \n \n(a) and (b):  The Ministry of Tourism under the schemes of \nSwadesh Darshan and PRASHAD (Pilgrimage Rejuvenation and \nSpiritual, Heritage Augmentation Drive) provides Central Financial \nAssistance to the State Governments/Union Territor y (UT) \n\nAdministrations for development of tourism infrastructure in the \ncountry. \n \nSubmission of project proposals by the State Governments/UT \nAdministrations under the above schemes is a continuous process. \nThe projects for development are identified in co nsultation with the \nState Governments/UT Administrations and are sanctioned subject \nto availability of funds, submission of suitable detailed projects \nreports, adherence to relevant scheme guidelines and utilization of \nfunds released earlier. Based on the above criteria, the Ministry has \nsanctioned following projects in Kerala including the project for \nMalabar region: - \n(Rs. in crore) \nS. \nNo. \nScheme/ \nYear of \nSanction \nName of the project Amount \nSanctioned \n1. Swadesh \nDarshan \n(2015-16) \n \n \nDevelopment of Pathana mthitta- Gavi- \nVagamon- Thekkady under Eco \nTourism Circuit in Idduki and \nPathanamthitta Districts \n76.55 \n2. Swadesh \nDarshan \n(2016-17) \nDevelopment of Sabarimala - Erumeli-\nPampa-Sannidhanam under Spiritual \nCircuit in      District Pathanamthitta \n99.99 \n3. Swadesh \nDarshan \n(2016-17) \nDevelopment of Sree \nPadmanabhaswamy- Arnamula- \nSabrimala under Spiritual Circuit  \n92.22 \n4. Swadesh \nDarshan \n(2018-19) \nDevelopment of Malanad Malabar \nCruise Tourism Project under Rural \nCircuit \n80.37 \n5. Swadesh \nDarshan \n(2018-19) \nDevelopment of  Sivagiri Sree \nNarayana Guru Ashram - Arruvipuram- \nKunnumpara Sree Subrahmania -  \nChembazhanthi Sree Narayana \nGurukulam under Spiritual Circuit \n69.47 \n6. Swadesh \nDarshan \n(2018-19) \nDevelopment of Kasaragod, Wayanad, \nKannur, Kozhikode, Palakkad, \nMallapuram, Thrichur, Ernakulam, \nIdukki, Kottayam, Allaphuza, \nPathananamithitta, Kollam, \nTrivandrum under Spiritual Circuit \n85.23 \n\n7. PRASHAD \n(2016-17) \nDevelopment at Guruvayur Temple 46.14 \nTotal 549.97 \n \nAll the above projects are at various stages of implementation. \n \n(c): The numbers of Foreign Tourist Arrivals (FTAs) and Domestic \nTourist Visits (DTVs) in the country during the last four years and \nthe current year along with the respective growth rates are as \nbelow:   \n \nYear FTAs (in \nmillion) \nAnnual \ngrowth in \nFTAs (%) \nDTVs (in \nmillion) \nAnnual growth \nin DTVs (%) \n2014 7.68 10.2 1282.8 12.3 \n2015 8.03 4.5* 1431.97 11.6 \n2016 8.80 9.7* 1615.39 12.8 \n2017 10.04 14.0* 1652.49 2.3 \n2018(P) 10.06 5.2* -- -- \n \n* The growth has been calculated in terms of absolute total \nP: Provisional \n \nThe State -wise details of funds sanctioned under Swadesh \nDarshan and PRASHAD Schemes in the country including Kerala are \ngiven at the Annexure. \n \n(d):  The Ministry of Tourism is aware of advisory/alerts issued by \nforeign countries to their citizens regarding their visits to India. To \naddress this issue, Overseas offices of the Ministry carries out \nregular interaction/ engagements with overseas tour operators, \ntravel agents, opinion makers, media and consumer, to keep them \nupdated about the ground situation in the country with an objective \nof reassuring them regarding travel to India. \n \n(e):  For creating conducive environment for tourists, the Ministry \nhas implemented facilities of E -Visa, WiFi connectivity at tourist \ndestinations, Web based public delivery system, 24X7 helpline \nservice, Safety and Security, Cleanliness at the tourist destinations \nin the country including Kerala. \n\n \nFor Promotion of Tourism, the Ministry undertakes several \npromotional activities in the dome"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |740", "t": "Multi-modal Logistics Parks", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 740 \n ANSWERED ON 7TH FEBRUARY, 2019 \n \n MULTI-MODAL LOGISTICS PARKS \n \n740.  Shri DUSHYANT  CHAUTALA  \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Govt. is planning a network of 35 multi - modal logistics parks with the aim to \nimprove the country’s logistics sector by lowering overall freight costs, reducing vehicular \npollution and congestion and cutting warehousing costs; \n(b) if so, the details thereof and whether the Government has also identified the locations for the \npurpose; and \n(c) if so, the details thereof and expected funds required for this purpose \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE  \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a)  Yes, Madam.   CCEA, in October 2017, has accorded in -principle approval for the \ndevelopment of 35 multimodal logistics parks as a part of the National Corridor Efficiency \nEnhancement Programme (NCEEP) under  Bharatmala Pariyojana to improve efficiency of the \nroad freight movement in the country. Logistics Parks will enable optimum and efficient \nvehicular movement in the country and thus lead to reduction in vehicular pollution and \ncongestion. Further, shifting warehouses, currently being operated inside city limits, to logistics \nparks will enable reduction in warehousing cost. In addition, modern and mechanized storage \nsolutions provided by logistics parks will enable reduction in storage and handling costs. \n \n(b) A network of 35 multimodal logistics parks has been identified and list of same as per \nBharatmala SOP dated 21.12.2017 is placed at Annexure-I. \n \n(c) Development of 35 multimodal logistics parks is part of Bharatmala Pariyojana and expected \nfunds required for development of Multi -modal Logistics Park is to be meet out from estimated \noutlay of Rs. 5,35,000 crore for Bharatmala Pariyojana as approved by CCEA. \n \n\nAnnexure I: \nList of Multimodal Logistics Parks \nS No Location \n1 Delhi – NCR (Delhi, Gurgaon, Ghaziabad, Faridabad, Noida) \n2 Mumbai (Mumbai, Mumbai Suburbs, JNPT, Mumbai Port, Raigad District) \n3 North Gujarat (Ahmedabad and Vadodara) \n4 Hyderabad \n5 South Gujarat (Surat and Bharuch) \n6 South Punjab (Ludhiana, Sangrur, Patiala) \n7 North Punjab (Amritsar, Jalandhar, Gurudaspur)  \n8 Jaipur \n9 Bangalore \n10 Pune \n11 Vijayawada \n12 Chennai \n13 Nagpur \n14 Indore \n15 Patna \n16 Kolkata \n17 Ambala \n18 Valsad \n19 Coimbatore \n20 Jagatsinghpur \n21 Nasik \n22 Guwahati \n23 Kota \n\nS No Location \n24 Panaji \n25 Hisar \n26 Visakhapatnam \n27 Bhopal   \n28 Sundargarh \n29 Bhatinda \n30 Solan \n31 Rajkot \n32 Raipur \n33 Jammu \n34 Kandla \n35 Cochin \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |742", "t": "Creation of Indian Sports Services", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 742 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \nCreation of Indian Sports Services \n \n742.     SHRI BHAGWANTH KHUBA: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) whether the Government proposes to introduce Indian \nSports Service to streamline the sports administration in \nthe country; \n(b) if so, the details and the present status thereof; \n(c) whether the Government has chalked out any roadmap in \nthis regard; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n[COL. RAJYAVARDHAN RATHORE (RETD.)] \n \n(a): No, Madam, \n \n(b) to (d):  Question does not arise. \n   \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |743", "t": "Accessibility of Drinking Water", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.743 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \nAccessibility of Drinking Water \n \n743. SHRI OM BIRLA: \nWill the Minister of DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION be pleased to state: \n(a) the percentage of households in the country whi ch have to travel more than half a \nkilometre to fetch drinking water;  \n(b) whether it is a fact that over 20 per cent of I ndians get their water from unsafe \nsources including untreated sources from the tap and uncovered wells; \n (c) if so, the reaction of the Government thereto; \n (d) whether it is a fact that less than 5 per cent  of households get their drinking water \nfrom the tap; and \n (e) if so, the measures taken to supply safe drinking water in every household in rural India? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION \n(SHRI RAMESH CHANDAPPA JIGAJINAGI) \n \n(a) This Ministry does not maintain information with re spect to ‘percentage of \nhouseholds, which have to travel more than half a k ilometer everyday to get \ndrinking water’. However, as per the Census 2011, 2 2.1% of the rural households \nhave to fetch drinking water from a distance of more than 500 meters in rural areas. \n \n(b) & (c) The Ministry categorizes the habitations as f ully covered habitations if at \nleast 40 liters per capita per day (LPCD) of safe w ater is available, partially \ncovered habitations if the availability of water is  less than 40 liters per capita per \nday (LPCD) and quality affected where quality of wa ter is chemically \ncontaminated. As reported by States on the online I ntegrated Management \nInformation System (IMIS), till date out of 17.19 L akhs total rural habitations in \nthe country, 80.61% rural habitations are fully cov ered, 15.82% habitations are \npartially covered and 3.56% habitations are quality affected.  \n \n(d) No, as reported by State Governments on IMIS, a s on date 18.05% of total \nrural households have tap connections. \n \n(e) Although Rural Drinking Water Supply is a State  subject, this Ministry \nsupplements the efforts of the State Governments fo r improving coverage of rural \ndrinking water supply by providing technical & fina ncial assistance through \nCentrally sponsored National Rural Drinking Water P rogramme (NRDWP) as per \nthe budgetary allocation for the same. Under NRDWP,  during 2018-19, Rs. \n5143.02 Crore have been released to various States. "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |744", "t": "Review of Drinking Water Schemes", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.744 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \nReview of Drinking Water Schemes \n \n744. DR. P.K. BIJU: \n \nWill the Minister of DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether the Government have reviewed the perfor mance of drinking water \nschemes and if so, the details and the outcome thereof; and \n (b) whether the Government has conducted any surve y regarding funds required \nfor various States/Union Territories, including Ker ala to provide safe drinking \nwater for all and if so, the details and the findings thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION \n(SHRI RAMESH CHANDAPPA JIGAJINAGI) \n \n(a) Every year between February and March, Annual Actio n Plan (AAP) meetings \nare held with the Departments of State Governments dealing with rural \ndrinking water supply, wherein the progress achieve d under different \ncomponents of National Rural Drinking Water program me (NRDWP) are \nreviewed and targets for the next financial year ar e fixed. The physical & \nfinancial progress of NRDWP is also reviewed in Nat ional / Regional / State \nlevel review workshops, meetingsand video-conferenc es. Further, the Ministry \nhas restructured NRDWP in November 2017 to make it more competitive, \noutcome based and result oriented where the focus i s on providing piped water \nsupply to all rural population and households.  \n \n(b) Funds under NRDWP are allocated to the States based  on various criteria \n[Rural population, Rural SC & ST population, Rural areas under Desert \nDevelopment Programme (DDP), Drought Prone Area Pro gramme (DPAP), \nHilly Area Development Programme (HADP) & special c ategory Hill States, \nPopulation residing in habitations affected by chem ical contaminants]. State / \nUT-wise details of funds released including the Sta te of Kerala till 03.02.2019 \nis at Annexure . \n \n \n\nAnnexure \nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (b) of Lok Sa bha Unstarred Q. No- 744 due for answer on \n07.02.2019 \n( Amount in Rs Crores ) \n  \nS.No.  State  \nFunds Released in 2018-\n19 till 03.02.19  \n1 ANDAMAN & NICOBAR 0.31 \n2 ANDHRA PRADESH 185.85 \n3 ARUNACHAL PRADESH 90.89 \n4 ASSAM 202.01 \n5 BIHAR 234.84 \n6 CHHATTISGARH 48.19 \n7 GOA 1.67 \n8 GUJARAT 222.27 \n9 HARYANA 76.76 \n10 HIMACHAL PRADESH 85.43 \n11 JAMMU & KASHMIR 212.46 \n12 JHARKHAND 80.82 \n13 KARNATAKA 233.44 \n14 KERALA 84.86 \n15 MADHYA PRADESH 243.62 \n16 MAHARASHTRA 239.06 \n17 MANIPUR 37.73 \n18 MEGHALAYA 49.15 \n19 MIZORAM 26.25 \n20 NAGALAND 17.36 \n21 ODISHA 77.5 \n22 PUDUCHERRY 0 \n23 PUNJAB 119.41 \n24 RAJASTHAN 655.41 \n25 SIKKIM 10.89 \n26 TAMIL NADU 123.41 \n27 TELANGANA 123.18 \n28 TRIPURA 51.73 \n29 UTTAR PRADESH 625.27 \n30 UTTARAKHAND 92.97 \n31 WEST BENGAL 890.28 \nTotal 5,143.02 \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |746", "t": "Flood Management", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES,\nRIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 746\nANSWERED ON 07.02.2019\nFLOOD MANAGEMENT\n746. SHRIMATI MEENAKASHI LEKHI\nWill the Minister of WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA\nREJUVENATION be pleased to state:\n(a) the detailed developments which have occurred under the agreement between Central Water\nCommission and Google for effective flood management;\n(b) the number of current flood assessment centres set up in the country, State/UT-wise;\n(c) whether the Central Water Commission’s flood monitoring and forecast dissemination was able to\naccurately predict the floods in Kerala; and\n(d) if so, the details thereof by indicating the number of advance days in this regard?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA\nREJUVENATION & PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS\n(SHRI ARJUN RAM MEGHWAL)\n(a) Central Water Commission (CWC) has signed a collaboration agreement with Google for improving\nflood prediction system. As per the agreement, CWC and Google will share technical expertise in the field\nof artificial intelligence, machine learning, geo -spatial mapping and analysis of hydrological obser vation\ndata to collaborate on (i) improving flood prediction systems, which will help provide location -targeted,\nactionable flood warnings, (ii) high priority research project utilizing Google Earth Engine to help\nvisualize and improve flood management and (iii) a cultural project to build online exhibitions on the\nRivers of India. The term of agreement is for three years.\n(b) The list of flood forecasting stations maintained by Central Water Commission in the country is given\nin Annexure-I.\n(c) & (d) The water level data of flood monitoring stations maintained by CWC in the State of Kerala\nwere uploaded in the Flood Forecasting Website of CWC. Further, Daily Flood Situation Report -cum-\nAdvisories (DFSRCA), based on the Indian Meteorological Department (IMD) rainfall predictions and the\nrainfall-runoff models were being issued in the year 2018. These advisories were disseminated to all\nstakeholders including Kerala State Disaster Management Authority through Facebook, Twitter, Disaster\nManagement Group of Ministry of Home Affairs. DFSRCA of 12th August 2018 conveyed that\n“Heavy to very heavy rainfall has been forecast for 13 th and 14th August in above areas, this rain\nmay lead to rise in water levels again in river Periyar, Bharathapuzha, Kabini, Cauvery and its\ntributaries. Since most of the dams are near Full Reservoir Level, maximum caution may be exercised\nwhile releasing excess water to downstream areas especially near sea mouth where there is chance of\nswell waves as warned by the Indian National Centre for Ocean Information System (INCOIS).”\nThis was issued 3 days in advance of the actual event of flood experienced in Kerala which started\nfrom 15 th August 2018 . These advisories were continued till the end of the flood spell indicati ng the\ndistricts affected as well as districts alerted in Kerala.\n*****\n\nANNEXURE-I\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b) OF UNSTARRED QUESTION\nNO. 746 TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 07.02.2019 REGARDING “ FLOOD\nMANAGEMENT”\nTable-1: State-wise Flood Forecasting Stations\nSl.\nNo. Name of State/UT\nNumber of flood forecasting Stations\nLevel Inflow Total\n1 Andhra Pradesh 8 9 17\n2 Arunachal Pradesh 2 0 2\n3 Assam 29 0 29\n4 Bihar 34 0 34\n5 Chattisgarh 1 0 1\n6 Diu & Daman 1 0 1\n7 Gujarat 6 6 12\n8 Haryana 1 1 2\n9 Himachal Pradesh 1 0 1\n10 Jammu & Kashmir 3 0 3\n11 Jharkhand 2 8 10\n12 Karnataka 1 9 10\n13 Madhya Pradesh 2 2 4\n14 Maharashtra 7 3 10\n15 NCT, DELHI 2 0 2\n16 Odisha 11 2 13\n17 Rajasthan 0 10 10\n18 Sikkim 0 1 1\n19 Tamil Nadu 3 10 13\n20 Telangana 5 6 11\n21 Tripura 2 0 2\n22 Uttar Pradesh 38 3 41\n23 Uttarakhand 4 2 6\n24 West Bengal 11 3 14\nTotal 174 75 249"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |747", "t": "GI Status", "head": " \n \nलोक सभा \nअताराांककत प्रश्न सांख्या 747 \nदिनाांक 07.02.2019 को उत्तर दिए जाने के ललए \n \nजीआई िजाा :  \n747:  श्री रवनीत लसांह : \n \nक्या वस्त्र मांरी यह बताने की कृपा करेंगे कक: \n(क) क्या पंजाब में केवल एक कढ़ाई उत्पाद को भौगोललक संकेत (जीआई) का दजाा ददया गया है, यदद हां, \nतो इसके क्या कारण हैं: \n(ख) सरकार की ओर से ववशेषकर पंजाब में टेक्सटाइल उत्पादों के ललए जीआई टैग के बारे में जागरूकता \nबढ़ाने के ललए क्या कदम उठाए गए हैं; और \n(ग) भारत में उन पारंपररक उत्पादों की संख्या का राज्य-वार ब्यौरा क्या है जजनमें जीआई टैग है? \n \nउत्तर \nवस्त्र राज्य मांरी \n(श्री अजय टम्टा) \n \n(क): जी हां महोदया। पंजाब में केवल एक कढ़ाई लशल्प अर्ाात फुलकारी को जीआई दजाा ददया गया है। \nइसके अलावा, दो लशल्पों नामश: पंजाबी जुत्ती और होलशयारपुर के जड़ाऊ काष्ठ के ललए पहले से ही \nआवेदन जमा ककए जा चुके  हैं जो जीआई रजजस्ट्रार के पास लंबबत है। \n \n(ख): सरकार ने संबंधित लशल्पों के ललए जीआई पंजीकरण तर्ा उपभोक्ता पंजीकरण के बारे में \nजागरुकता लाने के ललए देशभर में सभी 53 हस्ट्तलशल्प सेवा केन्द्रों में जीआई सहायता डेस्ट्क स्ट्र्ावपत \nककए हैं। इसके अलावा, भौगोललक संकेतकों के लाभों एवं जीआई के अन्द्य आयामों के बारे में जागरुकता \nलाने के ललए राष्रीय और क्षेत्रीय स्ट्तर पर लगातार कायाशालाएं आयोजजत की जा रही हैं। \n \n(ग):  92 पारंपररक हस्ट्तलशल्पों को जीआई टैग ददया गया है। सूची अनुबंि-1 पर संलग्न है। \n  \n\n \n \nअनुबांध-I \nक्रमाांक  जीआई लिल्प  राज्य \n1.  सुलेमानी पत्र्र, खंभात गुजरात  \n2.  एलेप्पी कॉयर  क े रल  \n3.  आंध्र प्रदेश की चमड़े की कठपुतली  आंध्र प्रदेश  \n4.  अरनमुला कन्द्नाडी  क े रल  \n5.  मध्य प्रदेश का बाघ वप्रंट  मध्य प्रदेश  \n6.  बागरु हस्ट्त ठप्पा छपाई  राजस्ट्र्ान  \n7.  बनारस गुलाबी मीनाकारी लशल्प  उत्तर प्रदेश  \n8.  बनारस िातु उभारदार (ररपोस्ट्से) लशल्प  उत्तर प्रदेश  \n9.  बस्ट्तर ढोकरा  छत्तीसगढ़  \n10.  बस्ट्तर लौह लशल्प  छत्तीसगढ़  \n11.  बस्ट्तर लकड़ी लशल्प  छत्तीसगढ़  \n12.  दततया एवं टीकमगढ़ के बेल िातु पात्र  मध्य प्रदेश  \n13.  बबदरी पात्र कनााटक  \n14.  जयपुर की नीली कुंभकारी  राजस्ट्र्ान  \n15.  बोबबली वीणा  आंध्र प्रदेश  \n16.  केरल का पीतल कशीदाकृत नाररयल खोल लशल्प  क े रल  \n17.  बुदीती बेल एवं तांबा लशल्प आंध्र प्रदेश  \n18.  चंबा रुमाल  दहमाचल प्रदेश  \n19.  चन्द्नापटना खखलौने एवं गुड़ड़या  कनााटक  \n20.  चेररयल धचत्रकारी  तेलंगाना  \n21.  चेट्टीनाड कोट्टन  तलमलनाडु  \n22.  फरुाखाबाद वप्रंट  उत्तर प्रदेश  \n23.  किरोज़ाबाद ग्लास  उत्तर प्रदेश  \n24.  मैसूर (कनााटक) क े  गंजीफा काडा  कनााटक  \n25.  गुलेदगुद्द खाना   कनााटक  \n26.  भदोही क े  हस्ट्ततनलमात कालीन  उत्तर प्रदेश  \n27.  जामनगर बांिनी  गुजरात  \n28.  कांगड़ा धचत्रकारी  दहमाचल प्रदेश  \n29.  कनााटक पीतल पात्र  कनााटक  \n30.  कश्मीर पेपर मैशी  जम्मू एवं कश्मीर  \n31.  कश्मीर सोज़नी लशल्प  जम्मू एवं कश्मीर  \n32.  कश्मीर अखरोट की लकड़ी पर नक्काशी  जम्मू एवं कश्मीर  \n33.  कश्मीर के हार् से गुंर्े कालीन  जम्मू एवं कश्मीर  \n34.  कसूती कशीदाकारी  कनााटक  \n35.  राजस्ट्र्ान की कठपुतली  राजस्ट्र्ान  \n36.  खाटमबंद  जम्मू एवं कश्मीर  \n37.  बबहार का खटवा पैच काया- एप्लीक बबहार  \n38.  खुजाा कुंभकारी  उत्तर प्रदेश  \n39.  ककनहल खखलौने  कनााटक  \n40.  कोणाका पत्र्र नक्काशी  ओड़डशा  \n41.  कोंडापल्ली बोम्माल्लू  आंध्र प्रदेश  \n42.  कच्छ कशीदाकारी  गुजरात  \n43.  इंदौर क े  चमड़े क े खखलौने  मध्य प्रदेश  \n44.  लखनऊ धचकन लशल्प  उत्तर प्रदेश  \n45.  लखनऊ जरदोज़ी  उत्तर प्रदेश  \n46.  मच्छलीपटनम कलमकारी  आंध्र प्रदेश  \n47.  पलाक्कड क े मडलम  क े रल  \n\n \n \n48.  मिुबनी धचत्रकारी  बबहार  \n49.  मोलेला लमट्टी काया  राजस्ट्र्ान  \n50.  मुरादाबाद िातु लशल्प  उत्तर प्रदेश  \n51.  मैसूर रोसवुड जड़ाऊ काया  कनााटक  \n52.  मैसूर लसल्क  कनााटक  \n53.  मैसूर पारंपररक धचत्रकारी  कनााटक  \n54.  नधचयरकोइल कुर्ुववल्लकू (नधचयरकोइल लैंप)  तलमलनाडु  \n55.  नक्शी कांर्ा   पजश्चम बंगाल  \n56.  तनमाल फनीचर  तेलंगाना  \n57.  तनमाल धचत्रकारी  तेलंगाना  \n58.  तनमाल खखलौने एवं लशल्प  तेलंगाना  \n59.  तनज़ामाबाद काली कुंभकारी  उत्तर प्रदेश  \n60.  ओड़डशा पट्टधचत्र ओड़डशा  \n61.  पट्टमदाई पाई (पट्टमदाई चटाई) तलमलनाडु  \n62.  पय्यान्द्नूर पववत्र ररंग  क े रल  \n63.  पेमबरर्ी िातु लशल्प  तेलंगाना  \n64.  फुलकारी पंजाब, हररयाणा, राजस्ट्र्ान  \n65.  वपपली एप्लीक काया ओड़डशा  \n66.  पुनेरी पगड़ी  महाराष्र  \n67.  सहारनपुर लकड़ी लशल्प  उत्तर प्रदेश  \n68.  सेलम फ े बिक  तलमलनाडु  \n69.  संदूर लंबानी कशीदाकारी  कनााटक  \n70.  सांगानेरी हस्ट्त ठप्पा छपाई  राजस्ट्र्ान  \n71.  संखेड़ा फनीचर  गुजरात  \n72.  शांतततनकेतन चमड़े की वस्ट्तुएँ  पजश्चम बंगाल  \n73.  केरल का स्ट्रू पाइन लशल्प  क े रल  \n74.  बबहार का लसक्की घास काया  बबहार  \n75.  करीमनगर का लसल्वर कफललग्री तेलंगाना  \n76.  सोलापुर टेरी टावल  महाराष्र  \n77.  श्रीकलाहस्ट्ती कलमकारी  आंध्र प्रदेश  \n78.  बबहार का सुजनी कशीदाकारी काया  बबहार  \n79.  सूरत ज़री लशल्प  गुजरात  \n80.  स्ट्वामीमलाई कांस्ट्य प्रततमाएँ  तलमलनाडु  \n81.  नागरकोइल के मंददर आभूषण  तलमलनाडु  \n82.  र्ंजावुर कलात्मक प्लेट  तलमलनाडु  \n83.  र्ंजावुर गुड़ड़या  तलमलनाडु  \n84.  र्ंजावुर धचत्रकारी  तलमलनाडु  \n85.  र्ंजावुर वीणा तलमलनाडु  \n86.  र्ेवा कला काया  राजस्ट्र्ान  \n87.  ततरुकनूर पेपर मैशी लशल्प   पुदुचेरी  \n88.  तोड़ा कशीदाकारी  तलमलनाडु  \n89.  वाराणसी के काँच क े  मनक े   उत्तर प्रदेश  \n90.  वाराणसी काष्ठ लेकरवेयर और खखलौने  उत्तर प्रदेश  \n91.  ववललयानुर टेराकोटा काया  पुदुचेरी  \n92.  वली धचत्रकारी  महाराष्र  \n \n********** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |748", "t": "Release of Funds from NSDF", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OFYOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.748 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \nRelease of Funds from NSDF \n \n748. SHRI KESINENI NANI:  \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) the details of target sports which have received funds from the \nNational Sports Development Fund (NSDF) during the last four years;  \n \n(b) the distribution of funds released from NSDF for Andhra Pradesh \nduring the said period, Sport-wise; and  \n \n(c) the details of infrastructure created at the district level in \nAndhra Pradesh utilizing the said fund? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n[COL. RAJYAVARDHAN RATHORE (RETD.)] \n \n(a): Assistance from National Sports Development Fund (NSDF)  \nhas been given during last four years to sportspersons for their \ncustomized training belonging to 22 sports disciplines  viz., \nathletics, archery, badminton, boxing, chess, cycling, fencing, golf, \ngymnastics, hockey, judo, sailing, shooting, squash, swimming, \ntable tennis, tennis, weightlifting, wrestling, wushu, para-sports and \nwinter sports.  The selected athletes are provided financial \nassistance for their customised training at Institutes having world \n\nclass facilities and other necessary support. The above list of sports \ndisciplines is inclusive of the sports disciplines, sportspersons of \nwhich have been assisted under Target Olympic Podium Scheme \n(TOPS), which is being implemented by the Ministry of Youth Affairs \n& Sports within overall ambit of NSDF.  \n \n(b):  Funds from NSDF are released to the sportspersons directly or \nto the coaches / academies associated with their customized \ntraining. State-wise details of sportspersons given assistance from \nNSDF are not maintained. Details of funds released sports-wise from \nNSDF during 2015-16 to 2018-19 are given in Annexure. \n \n(c): No financial assistance has been released from NSDF for \ncreation of infrastructure facilities at district level in Andhra \nPradesh.  \n  \n**** \n  \n\nANNEXURE \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (b) of Lok Sabha UnStarred \nQuestion No.748 to be answered on 07.02.2019 regarding Release of \nFunds from NSDF by Shri KesineniNani, Hon’ble Member of Parliament \n(Lok Sabha). \n \nDiscipline wise Assistance to Sportspersons under NSDF  \n(as on 31.12.2018) \n \nRs. in lakh  \nS No Discipline 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 \n   1 Archery 22.1 1.5 64 42.5 \n2 Athletics 171.53 90.16 104.38 87.5 \n3 Badminton 55.56 31.44 35 27.5 \n4 Boxing 40.94 17.27 52.5 63.5 \n5 Chess 6.33 13.51 9.45 38.58 \n6 Cycling   7.65 20.05 12.5 \n7 Fencing     3 2.5 \n8 Golf 2.34 3.95     \n9 Gymnastic 0.14   16.5 13.5 \n10 Hockey       18 \n11 Judo     14 9 \n12 Sailing 21.1 2.45   7 \n13 Shooting 367.36 206.65 111.28 89.5 \n14 Squash 39.79 8.38 16.75 7.5 \n15 Swimming 5.79 4.11 4.15 5 \n16 Table Tennis   0.57 19 15 \n17 Tennis 51.34 92.33 30.05 37.15 \n18 Weightlifting     40.5 13.5 \n19 Wrestling 34.68 60.82 38 23 \n20 Wushu     31.5 19.5 \n21 Para-Sports 64.71 84.47 85.32 67 \n22 Winter Games 19.07   29.34   \nTOTAL 902.78 625.26 724.77 598.83 \n \nFurther, NSDF has given block grant of Rs.35 crore to Sports Authority \nof India (SAI) for release of funds to sportspersons included in Target \nOlympic Podium Scheme (TOPS) for their customized training.  \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |749", "t": "Drinking Water Facility in Villages of Delhi", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.749 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \nDrinking Water Facility in Villages of Delhi \n \n749. SHRI PARVESH SAHIB SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether each village in Delhi has infrastructur e for door to door water supply, if so, \nthe steps taken to provide door to door water suppl y in rural areas of Delhi in the last \nfour years; and  \n(b) whether every village in Delhi has infrastructu re for providing the people access to \nclean drinking water and if so, the details thereof?  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION \n(SHRI RAMESH CHANDAPPA JIGAJINAGI) \n \n(a) & (b) As per information received from Delhi Ja l Board (DJB), the piped water \nsupply facility is available door to door in all ru ral villages except Badarpur Khadar \nunder Karawal Nagar constituency where it is techni cally not feasible to provide water \nsupply network. Water supply in this village is being maintained through water tankers. \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |75", "t": "Setting up of Spice Parks", "head": "Government of India \nMinistry of Youth Affairs & Sports \nDepartment of Sports \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 75 \nTO BE ANSWERD ON 07.02.2019 \n \nArchery Association of India \n \n*75. SHRI G. HARI: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH  AFFAIRS AND SPORTS  be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether it is a fact that the  World Archery Federation has  \nthreatened to suspend the Indian Archery  Federation/Archery \nAssociation of India over the outcome of the elections held recently; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) the steps taken/being taken by the Government to prevent such  \neventuality? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n[COL. RAJYAVARDHAN RATHORE (RETD.)] \n \n(a) to (c): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n_____________ \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c ) OF THE \nLOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 75 FOR REPLY ON 07.02.2019 \nASKED BY SHRI G. HARI REGARDING ARCHERY ASSOCIATION OF \nINDIA \n(a)& (b) As per email dated 16.01.2019 from World Archery \nFederation, addressed to the newly elected president of the Archery \nAssociation of India (AAI) they had, inter-alia, noted that the World \nArchery Executive Board cannot accept the outcome of the General \nAssembly held on the 22 nd December, 2018 and the election of the \nPresident and the rest of the Board since the constitution used to \nconduct the elections was never formally approved and only \naccepted by the Returning Officer. They had also asked for full \nminutes of the General Assembly of AAI for verification of the matter \nand informed that the World Archery Executive Board would take a \ndecision on the possible suspension of AAI after receipt of the \nminutes.  \nSubsequently, however, Mr. Tom Dielen, Secretary General, \nWorld Archery Federation, vide his email dated 23.01.2019, \naddressed to Secretary, Ministry of Youth Affairs & Sports, \nDepartment of Sports , sought certain clarifications relating to the \ngovernance of the Archery Association of India and especially to \ndecide what to do with the outcome of the elections  held on the \n22nd December 2018 and apprised that World Archery will take the \ntime necessary to come with a decision on the validity of the \nelections. \n(c) The matter of governance of AAI is sub-judice in the Hon’ble \nSupreme Court of India. The entire election process, including \nrevision of the constitution of the AAI, has been undertaken under \nthe directions of the Hon’ble Supreme Court of India , by a  duly \nappointed Administrator.  \nFurther, sports governance, both at the National and \ninternational level operates in an autonomous environment and the \nGovernment has no direct role in matters relating to affiliation of \nNational Sports Federations by their concerned World/continental \nbodies. Such matters are governed by the guidelines of the \nconcerned world/continental body. Thus, in order to obtain and/or \ncontinue the affiliation of the World Archery Federation, AAI has to \nfulfill the conditions laid down by the World body.  \n However, in response to the email dated 23.01.2019 from \nSecretary General, World Archery Federation, as mentioned in para \n\n(a) & (b) above, the Ministry of Youth Affairs & Sports, Department of \nSports has apprised him of the factual situation and informed him \nthat the Government is taking all necessary steps to resolve all \ncritical issues that may adversely affect players’ interests. Secretary \nGeneral, World Archery Federation, has acknowledged receipt of the \nreply of the Government.                  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |750", "t": "Check Gates and Toll Gates on NHs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 750 \nANSWERED ON 7TH FEBRUARY, 2019 \n \nCHECK GATES AND TOLL GATES ON NHS \n \n750. SHRI RADHESHYAM BISWAS: \n  \n Will the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  \n \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) the detail criteria of establishment  of  various  check  gates  on  National  Highways  (NHs)  \nincluding  toll  gates throughout the country; \n(b) whether the gates established by  the State Governments have been notified  by the Union \nGovernment; \n(c) if so, the details thereof; and \n(d) the total number of gates existing on  the  NHs,  State/UT-wise  including Assam? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a) to (c) Fee plazas are established on National Highways for collection of user fee as per the \napplicable National Highways (NH) Fee Rules 1997/2008. Government has notified the National \nHighways Fee (Determination of Rates & Collection) Rul es, 2008 on 05.12.2008, and the said rules, \nas amended from time to time, are applicable for determination of user fee for the projects executed \nand bids invited  on or after 05.12.2008. For the private funded projects  completed before 5th \nDecember, 2008 the fee collection is as per the provisions of the National Highways (collection of \nFees by any person for the use of Section of National Highways/Permanent Bridge/Temporary Bridge \non National Highways) Rules, 1997; and the National Highways (Rate of fee) Rules, 1997. However, \nNH Fee Rules 2008 are also applicable to public funded projects executed before 05.12.2008.  The \nuser fee on a stretch of National Highways is collected as per the individual Notifications published  \nin the Official Gazette by the Central Government.  In cases where a particular stretch of National \n\nHighway is entrusted to a State Government/UT, the executing authority of the concerned State \nGovernment/UT complies with the notification issued by the Central Government. \n \n(d) As on 31.12.2018, t he state-wise details of the  number of fee  plazas operated on  National \nHighways (NHs) are as under: \n \nS. No. State Number of Fee Plazas \n1. Andhra Pradesh 39 \n2. Assam 04 \n3. Bihar 17 \n4. Chhattisgarh 07 \n5. \nDelhi & EPE  \n(Eastern Peripheral Expressway) 11 \n6. Gujarat 36 \n7. Haryana 18 \n8. Jammu & Kashmir 05 \n9. Jharkhand 05 \n10. Karnataka 41 \n11. Kerala 03 \n12. Madhya Pradesh 38 \n13. Maharashtra 43 \n14. Odisha 11 \n15. Punjab 22 \n16. Rajasthan 77 \n17. Tamil Nadu 52 \n18. Telangana 15 \n19. Uttar Pradesh 48 \n20. Uttarakhand 02 \n21. West Bengal 17 \n \nTOTAL 511 \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |751", "t": "Transfer Orders of Employees of Prasar Bharati", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \nLOK SABHA    \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 751 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019) \n \nTRANSFER ORDERS OF EMPLOYEES OF PRASAR BHARATI \n751. SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE \n \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether there is rule to obtain permission from the Administrative \nDepartment of the Ministry to get stay order from the Hon’ble Court \nagainst the transfer orders of the employees of Prasar Bharati of Delhi \nto outside Delhi;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) the details of the employees who have sought permission along with \nthose who have not sought permission, Employee-wise; and  \n \n(d) the action taken by the Government against such employee s who have \nnot sought permission from the administration to file petition and to get \nstay order from the Hon’ble Court? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY \nOF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING  \n[COL RAJYAVARDHA RATHORE (Retd.)]  \n \n \n(a): No, Madam. \n(b) to (d): Question does not arise in view of (a) above.  \n \n \n*********** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |752", "t": "Funds Released under various Schemes", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 752 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07/02/2019 \n \nFUNDS RELEASED UNDER VARIOUS SCHEMES \n \n752.     SHRI RAMESH CHANDER KAUSHIK: \nSHRI KIRTI AZAD: \n \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING be pleased to state: \n \n(a)   the quantum of funds released to Sonepat in Haryana and Darbhanga in Bihar under \nvarious schemes of this Ministry, scheme-wise; \n \n(b)  whether the funds released  have been utilized under the respective schemes; \n \n(c)  if so, the details of the schemes under which the work has been completed or is near \ncompletion; and \n \n(d)  the details of the works pending along with the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF \nINFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \n \n[COL. RAJYAVARDHAN RATHORE (Retd.)] \n(a) to  (d): The schemes of Ministry of Information &  Broadcasting are Central Sector \nSchemes which aim at mass communication of the policies and programmes of the \nGovernment as well as entertainment and education. The benefits of such \nschemes/programmes/activities uniformly flow to the entire population. No funds of this \nMinistry are released to any State Government/District for implementing any Central \nSector Scheme. \n \n***** \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |754", "t": "Bid to Host Olympics", "head": " \n \nGovernment of India \nMinistry of Youth Affairs & Sports \nDepartment of Sports \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 754 \nTO BE ANSWERD ON 07.02.2019 \n \nBid to Host Olympics \n \n†754. SHRI HARISH CHANDRA ALIAS HARISH DWIVEDI: \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) whether the Government proposes to bid for hosting/organising \nOlympic games in the country;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the action taken by the \nGovernment in this regard; and \n(c) the details of infrastructure facilities required for organising the \nOlympic games in the country? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n[COL. RAJYAVARDHAN RATHORE (RETD.)] \n \n(a) Bidding to host multi-sports international events in India \nincluding Olympics is the responsibility of Indian Olympic \nAssociation (IOA). As per the guidelines issued by this Ministry, IOA \nhas to seek the approval of the Government before bidding for such \nevents. No specific proposal has been received in this Ministry \nrequesting the Government to grant permission for hosting the \nOlympics. \n \n(b)  Does not arise. \n \n(c) The requirement of infrastructure for organizing Olympics are \nfinalized once the Games are allotted to a country, with mutual \nconsultations between the host country, the International Olympic \nCommittee, the National Olympic Committee of the host country, \nand other stakeholders concerned.  \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |755", "t": "GPS Tracking System for Vehicles", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 755 \nANSWERED ON 07TH FEBRUARY, 2019 \n \nGPS TRACKING SYSTEM FOR VEHICLES \n \n755.  SHRIMATI RAKSHATAIKHADSE: \nSHRI ASADUDDINOWAISI: \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has made it mandatory to have GPS for all the public transport \nvehicles barring three wheelers and e -rickshaws w.e.f. 1st April, 2018 and if so, the details \nthereof;  \n(b) whether most of the States have not done much work on this issue, if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether any meeting with the States was held recently to implement the project; \n (d) if  so, the response of the Union Government and the steps taken or being taken by the \nGovernment in consultation with the States to implement the project; and  \n(e) whether the Union Government proposes to notify and make mandatory for all public \nvehicles to be equipped with GPS tracking device for safe transportation specially for \nchildren & women and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a) & (b)  Yes madam, Ministry of Road Transport and Highways has issued notification \nG.S.R 1095(E) dated 28.11.2016 mandating the provision of a vehicle location tracking device \nand one or more emergency buttons w.e.f. 01 stApril, 2018 in public service vehicles except two -\nwheelers, E-rickshaw, three wheelers and any transport vehicles for which permit is not required \nunder the Motor Vehicle Act, 1988. Various States and stakeholders brought to the notice of this \nMinistry that there are difficulties in implementing fitment Vehicle Location Tracking Device \nand Panic Buttons due to lack of command and control centers to monitor and track the vehicles. \nThe Ministry through notification No. S.O 1663(E) dated 18.04.2018 deferred the \nimplementation of Rule 125H for fitment of VLT and emergency button till 1st April,2019.  \n \n(c) to (e)  This Ministry vide S.O 5454 (E) dated 25th October, 2018, has mandated \ninstallation of vehicle location tracking device and emergency button  for new public service \nvehicle under rule 125H of the Central Motor Vehicle Rules, 1989 registered after 1 st January \n2019.Furtherall such public service vehicles registered upto the 31st day of December, 2018 the \nfitment of vehicle location tracking devic e and one or more emergency buttons , the concerned \nState or Union Territory Government may notify the date for compliance of requirements, in \ntheir respective State or Union Territory. \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |756", "t": "Details regarding NWQSM", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION  \n  \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 756  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019  \n  \nDetails regarding NWQSM \n \n756. SHRI ANTO ANTONY: \n \nWill the Minister of DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of objectives and salient features of t he National Water Quality Sub-\nMission (NWQSM) under National Rural Drinking Water Programme; \n \n(b) whether the State of Kerala is covered under the NWQSM; and \n \n(c) if so, give details, including the names of the pro jects being implemented under the \nNWQSM and the funds allocated so far, district-wise and amount-wise? \n \n \n \nANSWER  \nMINISTER OF STATE  \nIN THE MINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION  \n(SHRI RAMESH CHANDAPPA JIGAJINAGI) \n \n(a) The Ministry of Drinking Water had launched Nationa l Water Quality Sub-Mission \n(NWQSM) under National Rural Drinking Water Program me (NRDWP) on 22 nd  \nMarch, 2017 to provide safe drinking water to 27,54 4 arsenic / fluoride affected \nrural habitations, in a span of 4 years, subject to availability of funds.  \n \n(b) Number of arsenic / fluoride affected habitations a s reported by the States in \nIntegrated Management Information System (IMIS) of the Ministry as on 18 th  \nAugust, 2016 are considered under NWQSM. As reporte d by the Government of \nKerala, 73 fluoride affected habitations have been considered under NWQSM.  \n \n(c) As on 04 th  February, 2019, Rs. 4.43 Crore have been released to 04 schemes under \nNWQSM to Government of Kerala. Details are attached in Annexure.  \n \n****** \n  \n\nAnnexure: referred to in the part (c) of the reply to Lok Sabha Unstarred Question \nNo. 756 due for reply on 07/02/2019 \nDistrict-wise National Water Quality Sub-Mission schemes in Kerala State as on \n04.02.2019 \n \nS. \nNo.  \nDistrict \nName Block Name Panchayat \nName Project Name \n1 Alappuzha  Ambalapuzha Ambalapuzha \nWater Supply Scheme  to \nAmbalapuzha and Adj.Pts \n2 Palakkad Kollamkode Peruvemba \nAugmentation of Water Supply \nScheme to Peruvemba \n3 Palakkad Kuzhalmannam  Kannadi \nWater Supply Scheme  to \nKuzhalmannam - Kannadi - \nThenkuriisi Pts. \n4 Palakkad Nenmara Ayloor \nAugmentation of Water Supply \nScheme To Nenmara, Ayilur and \nMelarcode Phase I \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |757", "t": "Details regarding Artisans", "head": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.757 \nANSWERED TO BE ON 07.02.2019 \n \nDETAILS REGARDING ARTISANS: \n \n757:   SHRIMATI KAMLA DEVI PAATLE: \n \nWill be Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंरी   \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the number of artisans in the country, State-wise including Chhattisgarh; \n \n(b) the details of the welfare development programs/schemes launched for the artisans; \n \n(c) Whether there is any problem in the implementation of the development \nprograms/schemes for artisans; \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(e) the remedial measures being taken by the Government n this regard? \n \nउत्तर \nANSWER \nवस्त्र राज्य मंरी  (श्री अजय टम्टा) \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR TEXTILES \n(SHRI AJAY TAMTA) \n \n(a):  There are estimated 68.87 no. of artisans in the country.  Under Pahchan initiative 23.05 lakh  \nartisans have been mobilized so far. T he details of Pahchan identity cards issued to handicraft \nartisans, state wise including the state of Chhattisgarh are as per Annexure-I. \n \n(b): Office of The Development Commissioner (Handicrafts) has a separate scheme namely \nDirect Benefits to Artisans for Welfare of Artisans in which following components relate to social \nsecurity.  \n \nMudra Loan with Interest Subvention & Margin Money for Handicrafts Artisans \nUnder Pradhan Mantri Mudra Yojana (PMMY) Mudra Loan provided upto Rs.10 lakh to \nincome generating micro enterprises engaged in manufacturing trading and services sectors.  \nMudra Loans are being provided to provide adequate and timely assistance to artisans/weavers at \ninterest subvention of 6 % for a period of 3 year s to a maximum of Rs.100000/ - to meet their \ncredit requirements.  \n \nFurther to encourage the artisans to avail the facility of MUDRA loan, 20% of MUDRA \nloan amount is also being provided as Margin money  in their loan amount not exceeding to \nRs.10,000/-. Handicrafts Service Centres are facilitating artisans in availing the credit facility by \nmobilizing them, creating awareness & submitting applications to the Banks.  \n \nSupport to Artisans in Indigent Circumstances (Pension Scheme) \nThis scheme provides Financial Assistance to the aged awardees artisans who are the \nrecipient of Shilp Guru Award/ National Award/ Nation Merit Certificate hold/ State Award in \nhandicrafts and are not less than 60 years of age and their annual income should not be Rs. 50,000 \nor more. Finan cial assistance of Rs. 3,500/ - p.m. is given to Master Craftsperson in Indigent \nCircumstances.  \n \nInsurance Scheme for Handicrafts Artisans \nBima Yojana for Handicrafts Artisans under Pradhan Mantri Jeevan Jyoti Bima Yojana \n/Pradhan Mantri Surkasha Bima Yojana for the age group of 18 to 50 years and Modified Aam \nAdmi Bima Yojana for the age group of 51 to 59 years who were enrolled as on June, 2017. \n \n \n \n \n\n \nThe artisans enrolled under the scheme is provided insurance protection through Life Ins urance \nCorporation of India as per details given below :- \n \n \nFor the age group of 18 to 50 years. \n \n- Rs.2 lakh is payable on beneficiary's death due to any cause, for one year period from 1 st June \nto 31st May.  \n \n- Risk coverage available will  be Rs.2.00 lakh for accidental death and per manent total \ndisability and Rs.1.00 lakh for partial disability for one year period from 1st June to 31st  May. \n \nFor the Age group of 51 to 59 years \nBENEFITS \nNatural Death Rs.  60,000/- \nAccidental Death Rs.1,50,000/- \nTotal disability Rs.1,50,000/- \nPartial Disability Rs.   75,000/- \n \nMOUs with NIOS & IGNOU \nA MOU has been signed between Govt. and National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS) Indira \nGandhi National Open University (IGNOU) for collaboration in the area of education for \nhandicraft artisans and their children wherein reimbursement of 75% of the fee  for SC/ST/BPL \nand women artisans is being done.  \n \n(c) to (e): The schemes of “National Handicraft Development Programme [NHDP]”  & \nComprehensive Handicrafts Cluster Development Scheme (CHCDS)  are being implemented for \nthe benefit of handicrafts artisans without any problem so far. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nANNEXURE- I \nState - wise Artisans Mobilized \nStates Artisans \nUttar Pradesh 870316 \nUttarakhand 31814 \nAndhra Pradesh 54568 \nTelangana 33455 \nKarnataka 24659 \nKerala 38478 \nTamil Nadu 35619 \nPondicherry 13018 \nA&N Island 1765 \nRajasthan  97047 \nDelhi 14865 \nPunjab 27584 \nHaryana 30746 \nHimachal Pradesh  12531 \nJ & K 91143 \nMadhya Pradesh 83019 \nGujarat 112518 \nMaharastra 46220 \nChhattisgarh  12908 \nGoa 9478 \nTripura 10507 \nMizoram  3260 \nAssam 70172 \nSikkim 2312 \nArunachal Pradesh 6590 \nNagaland 5264 \nManipur 69418 \nMeghalaya 2716 \nWest Bengal 230965 \nOdisha 110785 \nJharkhand 36335 \nBihar 115070 \nTotal  2305145 \n \n******** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |758", "t": "PMGSY", "head": " \nO.I.H. \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 758 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \n PMGSY  \n \n758.  SHRI MANSUKHBHAI DHANJIBHAI VASAVA:  \n SHRI HARISHCHANDRA CHAVAN: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether a majority of the work approved under P radhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana \n(PMGSY) have not been completed due to forest related rules and have been cancelled;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof in respect of Narmad a and Bharuch district of Gujarat;  \n(c) the steps taken/being taken by the Government t o provide civic amenities like housing \nand road in tribal areas of the country; \n  \n(d) the action taken/being taken by the Government to relax the rules proving a hindrance in \nimplementation of the said yojana; and  \n(e) the outcome thereto?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI RAM KRIPAL YADAV) \n \n(a)& (b): Since inception till 05.02.2019, out of 1 ,77,973 road/bridge works sanctioned \nunder Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) 1,48 ,963 road/bridge works have been \ncompleted. As reported by the States, 277 road work s have been dropped so far due to non-issue \nof forest clearance. In the State of Gujarat, 5 roa d works have been dropped under PMGSY due \nto non-issue of forest clearance. \n \nAs reported by the State Government of Gujarat, no road works of PMGSY has been dropped \ndue to forest related rules in respect of Narmada and Bharuch district of Gujarat. \n \n(c)to (e): PMGSY is an area development programme a nd the unit of programme is a \nhabitation. PMGSY is not an individual beneficiary oriented scheme and target of the \nprogramme is to connect the eligible habitations wi th roads constructed under it catering to the \naccess needs of the entire population of the target  habitation. However, relaxation has been \nprovided to the Tribal (Schedule V) areas and Selec ted Tribal and Backward Districts (as \nidentified by the Ministry of Home Affairs (MHA) an d the erstwhile Planning Commission), and \n\nunconnected habitations in these areas with a popul ation of 250 persons and above in the Core \nNetwork as per Census 2001 are eligible for connectivity under the scheme.  \n \nThe Pradhan Mantri Awaas Yojana-Gramin (PMAY-G) aim s at providing financial assistance \nfor construction of Pucca Houses to all Houseless a nd Household living in zero,  one or two \nroom kutcha houses with kutcha wall and kutcha roof in the rural areas of the country. \n \nAt the National Level, 60% of the target allocated to each State/Union Territories (UTs) is \nearmarked for Schedule Caste (SC) / Schedule Tribe (ST) subject to availability of eligible \nPMAY-G beneficiaries in the Permanent Wait List (PW L) of PMAY-G. Within earmarked \ntargets, the proportion of SC and ST is to be decid ed from time to time by the respective \nStates/UTs. The States/UTs are allowed to interchange targets between SC and ST if there are no \neligible beneficiaries from either of the category and it is certified as such. Household from \nPrimitive Tribal Groups are automatically included in the universe of eligible beneficiaries under \nPMAY-G. \n \nSince inception till 6 \nth  February, 2019, 1, 45,555 habitations have been pr ovided connectivity \nthrough all-weather roads, including eligible habit ations in the tribal areas of Country. Under \nPMAY-G, 17,28,755 house sanctioned to ST Category h ave been completed during the years \n2016-17, 2017-18 and 2018-19  till date. \n \n \n***** \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |759", "t": "Construction of NHs", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 759 \nANSWERED ON 7TH FEBRUARY, 2019 \n  \nCONSTRUCTION OF NHS \n \n759.  SHRI J.J.T. NATTERJEE:  \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसडक परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is constantly reviewing National Highways (NHs) works across \nthe country, if so, the details thereof; \n(b) whether more than 300 projects  were identified which will be over by 2019,  achieving \nthe highest ever construction in the financial year 2018-19, if so, the details thereof; \n(c) the list of States where more NHs have been constructed during the last 4 years; \n(d) whether the Government has any  plan to improve the construction rate of  the de layed \nprojects; and \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n(a)  Yes Madam. Review meeting s have been continuously going on at various level  with the \nofficials of Ministry, State PWDs, officials of other ministries, contractors, etc.   \n \n(b) Ministry has targeted this year to be the construction year with enhanced progress in many \nNational Highways works along with the progress which will be coming out from the projects \nwhich are going to be completed by March 2019.  And 295 projects have been identified for \ncompletion by the end of March 2019. \n \n(c) State -wise construction of National Highways during the last four year is given at  the \nAnnexure-I.   \n \n(d) to (e) To expedite completion of pending NHs projects various steps are taken which include \nstreamlining of land acquisition & environment clearances, premium re -scheduling, close \ncoordination with other Ministries, revamping of dispute resolution mechanism, frequent reviews \nat various levels etc.  In order to ensure ti mely completion of the projects , regular meetings are \nheld with project developers, State Governments and contractors at all levels. \n \n\nANNEXURE-I \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN PART OF (c) OF REPLY TO LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 759 FOR ANSWER ON 07.02.2019 ASKED BY SHRI J.J.T. NATTERJEE \nREGARDING CONSTRUCTION OF NHS. \n \nThe State /UT-wise details of length of NHs constructed during each of the last four years \nSr. \nNo. State / UT Length completed (in km) \n2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 \n1 Andhra Pradesh 136 462 402 459 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 88 80 174 188 \n3 Assam 178 87 165 305 \n4 Bihar 115 181 400 343 \n5 Chandigarh 1 0 0 0 \n6 Chhattisgarh 307 327 483 522 \n7 Delhi 0 0 0 139 \n8 Goa 0 2 4 20 \n9 Gujarat 139 277 86 189 \n10 Haryana 86 170 369 291 \n11 Himachal Pradesh 34 100 72 135 \n12 Jammu & Kashmir 57 34 33 162 \n13 Jharkhand 126 119 211 238 \n14 Karnataka 130 314 656 769 \n15 Kerala 29 10 46 16 \n16 Madhya Pradesh 335 306 475 594 \n17 Maharashtra 124 324 750 1,338 \n18 Manipur 46 6 4 231 \n19 Meghalaya 88 50 6 48 \n20 Mizoram 5 15 88 43 \n21 Nagaland 13 25 4 4 \n22 Odisha 386 268 490 554 \n23 Puducherry 14 22 8 17 \n24 Punjab 115 154 384 357 \n25 Rajasthan 853 1,063 1,125 1,074 \n26 Sikkim 30 0 0 45 \n27 Tamil Nadu 58 237 469 307 \n28 Telangana 171 222 113 161 \n29 Tripura 18 0 42 87 \n30 Uttar Pradesh 542 669 584 695 \n31 Uttarakhand 49 335 204 256 \n32 West Bengal 138 203 386 222 \n33 A&N Islands 0 0 0 21 \nTotal 4,410 6,061 8,231 9,829 \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |76", "t": "Smart Schools", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \n     LOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 76 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \nSmart Schools \n  \n†76.   SHRIMATI REKHA VERMA: \n \n         Will the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the number of schools upgraded by the Government  as smart schools under th e Saansad Adarsh Gram \nYojana, State/ UT-wise;  \n(b) the details of upgradation works carried out in pr imary and upper primary schools in the villages so far \nadopted by the Members of the Parliament under the Saansad Adarsh Gram Yojana;  \n(c) whether any assessment has been conducted in order to improve the quality of education in such schools;  \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and  \n(e) if not, the reasons therefor?  \n ANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n  (DR. SATYA PAL SINGH) \n \n(a) ICT interventions have been approved for 434 sec ondary and senior secondary schools in Sansad Adarsh \nGrams till 2018-19. The State/UT-wise list is enclosed at Annexure-I. \n \n(b) 25 schools have been upgraded from primary to upper primary in the Sansad Adarsh Grams. Further, 51 \nschools have been upgraded from upper primary to secondary  till 2018-19. The State/UT-wise list is enclosed at \nAnnexure-II & Annexure-III respectively. \n \n(c) to (e) Under the schemes, besides regular monito ring of physical and financial progress of approved \ninterventions through monthly reports, periodic review meetings, scrutiny of audit reports, etc., capacity building \nof States/UTs is taken up through orientation workshops  and development of exemplar training packages etc. \nThe National Achievement Survey for Class X for the fi rst time was conducted in 2015 on a sample comprising \nof 2,77,416 students of 7,216 schools across 34 States/UTs and Boards. The achievement level of students of \nclass X was studied in 5 subjects, i.e. English, Mathem atics, Social Science, Science and Modern Indian \nLanguage.  The survey also studied difference in achieve ments level of class X students with regard to area, \ngender, social group, school board and management of school. The report of the survey is available at the \nNCERT's website (http://www.ncert.nic.in/). National Ac hievement Survey (NAS) was also conducted on 13th \nNovember, 2017 through which the lear ning levels of around 22 lakh students of Classes III, V and VIII from \n1.10 lakh schools across 701 districts in all 36 States a nd UTs were assessed. In th e survey, the students of \nClasses III and V were assessed on Reading Comprehension,  Mathematics and Environmental Studies and Class \nVIII students were assessed on Language, Maths, Scienc e and Social Science. This competency based \nassessment was based on the Learning Outcomes developed by the National Council of Educational Research \nand Training (NCERT). Along with the test items, qu estionnaires pertaining to students, teachers and schools \nwere also used. District report cards for NAS 2017 have  been released and are available on MHRD website and \nhave also been shared with the Hon’ble Members of Parliament. Similarly, the Cycle-2 of National Achievement \nSurvey for Class-X has been conducted on 5th February, 2018 at the district level with a sample size of 15.5 lakh \nstudents. \n \nDuring 2018-19, many modules for the post NAS interventions have been initiated which includes understanding \nthe district report cards, pedagogical inputs to target the learning outcomes, school based assessment, promoting \nexperiential learning, sports and art integrated education and improving community participation.  \n \n*****  \n\n \nAnnexure – I \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 76 TO BE  ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 ASKE D BY SHRIMATI REKHA \nVERMA REGARDING “SMART SCHOOLS” \n \nSl \nNo \nName of State/UT  No of ICT Schools \napproved in Sansad \nAdarsh Grams \n1 Andaman And Nicobar Islands 3 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 26 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 1 \n4 Assam 28 \n5 Bihar 19 \n6 Chhattisgarh 7 \n7 Dadra and Nagar Haveli 2 \n8 Daman and Diu 1 \n9 Goa 2 \n10 Gujarat 23 \n11 Haryana 18 \n12 Himachal Pradesh 5 \n13 Jammu and Kashmir 6 \n14 Jharkhand 9 \n15 Karnataka 16 \n16 Kerala 65 \n17 Lakshadweep 2 \n18 Madhya Pradesh 16 \n19 Maharashtra 41 \n20 Manipur 1 \n21 Mizoram 3 \n22 Nagaland 6 \n23 Odisha 28 \n24 Puducherry 3 \n25 Punjab 13 \n26 Rajasthan 31 \n27 Sikkim 2 \n28 Tamil Nadu 29 \n29 Telangana 3 \n30 Tripura 3 \n31 Uttar Pradesh 10 \n32 Uttrakhand 3 \n33 West Bengal 9 \n             Total=434 \n \n \n \n  \n\n \n \n \n \n \nAnnexure – II \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 76 TO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 ASKED BY SHRIMATI REKHA VERMA \nREGARDING “SMART SCHOOLS” \nS.no. Name of \nState/UT \nDistrict Gram Panchayat Number of schools \nupgraded from \nprimary to upper \nprimary  \n1 Gujarat Dohad Mundha 1 \n2 Maharashtra Pune Vadgaon-shinde 1 \n3 Rajasthan Tonk Kantoli 1 \n4 Tamil Nadu Namakkal Thinnanur Nadu 1 \n5 Tam"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |760", "t": "Construction of NH 58-E", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 760 \nANSWERED ON 07TH FEBRUARY, 2019 \n \nCONSTRUCTION OF NH 58-E \n \n760. SHRI ARJUN LAL MEENA:  \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has started work of National Highway (NH) No. 58 -E \nsmoothly; \n(b) if so, the details of the amount allocated for this highway;  \n(c) whether compensation has been provided to the people whose lands were acquired to \nconstruct this highway;  \n(d) if so, the details thereof; \n(e) the time by which the compensation will be provided to people who haven’t received it \nso far; and  \n(f) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY \n OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n \n \n(a) & (b) Yes, Madam. Works of upgradation and widening to 2 lane with paved shoulders of \nNational Highway (NH) No. NH 58E from km 0/0 to 91/0 has already commenced. Total \nsanctioned cost is Rs 712 crore. \n \n(c)  to (f ) Yes, Madam. An amount of Rs. 121.567 crore has been deposited with the \nCompetent Authority for Land Acquisition (CALA) Girwa & Jhadol for disbursement against \n307.88 Ha of l and acquisition, out of which Rs. 32.47 crore has been disbursed and the \nbalance disbursement is expected within two months. \n***** \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |761", "t": "Setu-Bharatam Programme", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT & HIGHWAYS \nLOK    SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 761 \nANSWERED ON 07THFEBRUARY, 2019 \n \n \nSETU-BHARATAM PROGRAMME \n \n \n761.    DR. BANSHILAL MAHATO: \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \n   be pleased to state: \n \n(a)     whether the Government has launched Setu-Bharatam Programme for construction of   \nbridges and over bridges on national highways across the country, if so, the details \nthereof;  \n (b)     whether the Government proposes to provide grants to States and Union Territories for     \ndevelopment of roads and bridges under the schemes;  \n(c)   if so, the details thereof along with the criteria for providing funds under the said     \nscheme;  \n  (d)     the details of proposals submitted by various State Governments in this regard during  the           \nlast three years, State/UT-wise; \n     (e)     the details of sanctioned construction work in the country, project/ State-wise; and  \n(f)      the details of the expenditure incurred on construction and maintenance of bridges and             \nnew bridges on National Highways in the country during the last three years, State-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n \n (a) to (f) Till date 9 3 number of Road Over Bridges / Road Under Bridge (ROBs/ RUBs) \nhave been sanctioned under Setu-Bharatam. State-wise details of sanctioned ROBs/RUBs are \nplaced at Annexure. There are difficulties  in getting land for approaches of ROBs/RUBs \nespecially in built up areas. Moreover, the cost of acquisition of such land is also very high. \nMinistry has, therefore, decided that priority would be accorded to those ROBs/RUBs where \nno land acquisition is in volved or to adopt the Grand Challenge Mechanism to take up \nROBs/RUBs where land is made available by the State Government, at its own cost. Ministry \nallocates funds for the development of NHs State/UT- wise and not project –wise. \n\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN R EPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (f) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.761 FOR ANSWER ON 07 th FEBRUARY, 2019 ASKED \nBY DR. BANSHILAL MAHATO REGARDING \"SETU-BHARATAM PROGRAMME\" \n \nState Wise number of ROB/RUB sanctioned under Setu-Bharatam \nState Numbers \nAndhra Pradesh 19 \nBihar 14 \nChattisgarh 1 \nGujarat 1 \nHaryana 6 \nKarnataka 7 \nMadhya Pradesh 2 \nOdisha 4 \nPunjab 10 \nRajasthan 7 \nUttarakhand 2 \nUttar Pradesh 1 \nWest Bengal 19 \nTotal 93 \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |762", "t": "Payment of Recoveries to NHDC Ltd.", "head": " \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 762 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \nPayment of Recoveries to NHDC Ltd. \n \n762: SHRI HARISHCHANDRA CHAVAN \n SHRI RAM TAHAL CHOUDHARY  \n \nWill the Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंरी   \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the payment of various recoveries has not been made to National \nHandloom Development Corporation Ltd. (NHDC); \n(b) if so, the recovery-wise details thereof; \n(c) if not, the reasons for no recovery till date; and \n(d) the number of Officers held responsible in this regard along with  the  \ndetails of action taken against them? \n \n \nउत्तर \nANSWER \nवस्त्र राज्य मंरी  (ाी ट य ी ीा)  \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR TEXTILES \n(SHRI AJAY TAMTA) \n \n \n(a) to (c) Indian Overseas Bank Indira Nagar, Lucknow had debited a sum of \nRs 6.61 crore twice in the account of NHDC, Lucknow Office on 14th May 2018 \nagainst Single RTGS payment advice and remitted the amount in favour of 11 \nyarn suppliers. Rs 3.74 crore has been recovered and efforts are being made to \nrecover balance amount of Rs 2.87 crore. \n \n(d) Administrative action has been initiated against three officials of NHDC \nwho were prima facie involved in these irregularities. \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |764", "t": "Investment in Energy Sector", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENRGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 764 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \nINVESTMENT IN ENERGY SECTOR \n \n764. SHRI RAM CHARAN BOHRA \n \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to formulate any scheme for investment in the Renewable Energy \nSector;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) the amount of allocated fund spent on the renewable energy schemes during the last three years;  \n(d) if so, the details thereof;  \n(e) if not, the reasons therefor;  \n(f) the target fixed in terms of Megawatt for the renewable energy production; and  \n(g) the total quantity of electricity distributed every year from the said production? \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER (I/C) \n(SHRI R. K. SINGH) \n \n(a) & (b) The Government is already implementing various programs/schemes for promotio n of grid \ninteractive renewable energy such as solar, wind, bio -power and small hydro power in the country. The \ndetails of major steps taken by the Government to attract investment in the renewable energy sector are \nas follows:- \n \ni. Waiver of Inter State T ransmission System (ISTS) charges and losses for inter -state sale of solar \nand wind power for projects to be commissioned up to March, 2022. \nii. Permitting Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) up to 100 percent under the automatic route. \niii. Notification of st andard bidding guidelines to enable distribution licensee to procure solar and \nwind power at competitive rates in cost effective manner. \niv. Declaration of trajectory for Renewable Purchase Obligation (RPO) up to the year 2022. \nv.  Implementation of Green Energy Corridor project to facilitate grid integration of large scale \nrenewable energy capacity addition.   \n \n(c), (d) & (e) The details of funds allocated and released as Central Financial Assistance (CFA) for the \ndevelopment of renewable energy schemes in the country during the last three years are as follows:- \n                                                                                                      (Rs in Cr) \nYear Fund Allocated at RE stage Plan Expenditure \n2016-17 4307.00 3870.97 \n2017-18 4040.60 3731.91 \n2018-19 (up to December, 2018) 5105.80 3500.50 \n \n(f) The Government has set a target of installing 175000 MW of renewable energy capacity by the year \n2022 which includes 100000 MW from solar, 60000 MW from wind, 10000 MW from bio -power and \n5000 MW from small hydro power.  \n \n(g) The details of generation of el ectricity through renewable sources of energy during the last three \nyears are as follows:- \nYear Generation in billion units (BU) \n2016-17 81.54 \n2017-18 101.83 \n2018-19 (up to December, 2018) 97.92 \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |765", "t": "Payment of Wages under MGNREGS", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 765 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \n PAYMENT OF WAGES UNDER MGNREGS  \n \n765.  SHRI JANARDAN SINGH SIGRIWAL: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether suggestions have been received from var ious quarters for payment of wages in \ncash to workers under Mahatma Gandhi National Rural  Employment Guarantee Scheme \n(MGNREGS);  \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n  \n(c) whether the demand for employment under MGNREGS  has come down;  \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and  \n(e) the corrective steps taken by the Government in  this regard?  \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI RAM KRIPAL YADAV) \n \n(a): \nNo Madam. \n \n(b): Does not arise. \n \n \n(c)to (e): The Labour Budget (persondays) and expen diture under MGNREGA are on an \nincreasing trend. The details of budget allocation and agreed to Labour Budget (persondays) \nduring the last two years and current financial year 2018-19 (as on 04.02.2019) are given below: \n(In crore) \nFinancial Year Budget \nAllocation (In Rs.) \nAgreed to \nLabour Budget (persondays) \n2016-2017 48,220.26 220.93 \n2017-2018 55,167.06 231.31 \n2018-2019  \n(As on 04.02.2019) 61,084.09 247.16 \nSource: www.nrega.nic.in  \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |766", "t": "Incidence of Derogatory Remarks", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 766 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07/02/2019  \n  \nINCIDENCE OF DEROGATORY REMARKS \n \n766.  SHRI SHIV KUMAR UDASI: \n \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING   \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether there is increase in incidence of derogatory remarks by one political \nparty leaders to another in the country;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether the Government proposes to take any action against these leaders and \nif so, the details thereof; and  \n(d)  the steps taken by the Government to stop such incidence and if not, the reasons \ntherefor? \n  \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF \nINFORMATION & BROADCASTING      \n[COL RAJYAVARDHAN RATHORE (Retd.)]  \n \n(a) to (d ): There is no study/report in the notice of this Ministry indicating increased \nincidents of derogatory remarks by one political party leaders against an other. The \nProgramme Codes under the Cable Television Networks Rules, 1994, inter alia, provide \nthat no programme should be carried out on the TV which “criticises, maligns or \nslanders any individual in person or certain groups, segments of social, public, moral life \nof the country”. Further, under the Press Council Act, 1978, persons can mak e \ncomplaint to the Council relating to publication of matter in newspaper which is \nconsidered offensive or is not in public taste, under Section 14 of the said Act.  \n        \n             As and when matters relating to violation/infringement of the aforeme ntioned \nprovisions are brought to the notice of the Ministry, appropriate action under the law is \ntaken.   \n********* "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |767", "t": "Details regarding CBI Inquiry", "head": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 767 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \nDETAILS REGARDING CBI INQUIRY \n \n767. SHRI P.K. KUNHALIKUTTY: \n \n     Will the Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंरी   \nbe pleased to state? \n \n(a) the details of bullion parties against whom CBI have sought details since 2014-\n15. Company-wise and the clarifications received from CBI before releasing \npayments to small bullion parties against whom no case is pending as on 31st \nJanuary, 2014: and \n \n(b) the reasons for withholding payments of small bullion parties who have \ncompleted their agreements in 2014 and have no investigation pending as on \n31.12.2014? \n \nउत्तर \nANSWER \nवस्त्र राज्य मंरी  (श्री अजय टम्टा) \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR TEXTILES \n(SHRI AJAY TAMTA) \n \n(a) & (b):  Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI) has registered two cases against the \nbullion parties of M/s Edelweiss Commodities Ltd. (ECL) and Aaryavart \nCommodities Pvt. Ltd (ACPL).  While HHEC had submitted that this i s as per \ncommercial arrangement and as per the business module adopted by other bulli on \nimporting nominated agencies, CBI is examining the issue  of availing buyer’s \ncredit. Bullion parties whose payments have been withheld by (HHEC)  have \nfollowed the process of imports as per  agreements which are identical to the \nagreement signed between ECL and HHEC . HHEC has sought vi ews of CBI with  \nregard to withholding  payment of the bullion parties other than M/s Edelweiss \nCommodities Ltd. (ECL). However, no response has been received.  \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |768", "t": "Energy Skill University", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENRGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 768 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \nENERGY SKILL UNIVERSITY  \n \n768. COL. SONARAM CHOUDHARY \n \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the locations of energy skill related universities in the country and their features; \n(b) whether Western Rajasthan is wind and solar energy hub in the country; \n(c) if so, the details thereof;   \n(d) whether the Government has received proposals to open Barmer (Rajasthan) energy skill \nuniversity;   \n(e) if so, the details thereof;   \n(f) whether the Government  intends to open energy skill university in Barmer (Rajasthan); \nand  \n(g) if so, the time by when it is going to open? \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER (I/C) \n(SHRI R. K. SINGH) \n \n(a) There are no energy skill related universities in the country. However,  a number of the \nUniversities/ Deemed Universities / Institutes in the country offer M.Tech/ M.Sc Programmes \nin the energy studies/ renewable energy. Renewable energy is also one of the electives in \nundergraduate course curriculum at B.Tech level. \n \n(b) & (c) Rajasthan has good wind and solar resource and therefore has good potential for \nwind and solar  energy projects. A capacity of about 4.3 GW from wind energy has so far \nbeen installed majorly in the western districts of Rajasthan i.e Jaisalmer, Jodhpur and Barmer. \nSix solar parks have also been approved in the state of Rajasthan for setting up of gri d \nconnected ground mounted solar projects as detailed below: \nName of Solar Park Capacity (in MW) \nBhadla Phase-II Solar Park; Jodhpur 680 \nBhadla III Solar Park, Jodhpur 1000 \nBhadla IV Solar Park, Jodhpur 500 \nPhalodi-Pokaran Solar Park 750 \nFatehgarh Phase 1B Solar Park, Jaisalmer 421 \nNokh Solar Park, Jaisalmer 980 \nTotal Solar Parks (6) 4331 \n(d) to (g) No specific proposal has been received in the Ministry of New and Renewable \nEnergy to open Barmer (Rajasthan) Energy Skill University. However, the Ministry of Skill \nDevelopment and Entrepreneurship (MSDE) is supporting  a proposal with Hydrocarbon \nSector Skill Council as nodal point, to set -up an Energy Skill Development Campus near \nPachpedra Refinery in Barmer, Rajasthan under Rajasthan ILD Skills Un iversity (RISU) \nJaipur to develop local human resource by providing skill-based knowledge and making them \nemployable for the skilled jobs to be generated at petroleum refinery. No separate Energy \nSkill University is envisaged in Barmer by the Ministry of New and Renewable Energy. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |769", "t": "Land Acquisition under Sagarmala Programme", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF SHIPPING\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 769\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 7TH FEBRUARY, 2019\nLAND ACQUISITION UNDER SAGARMALA PROGRAMME\n769. SHRI A.P JITHENDER REDDY:\nWill the Minister of SHIPPING be pleased lo state:\ndm qR-*e-c q*\n(a) whether the Government is facing certain rssues regarding land acquisition to\naccomplish the Sagarmala programme and if so, the details thereof and the\nquantum of area under dispute, State-wise;\n(b) whether it is true that no container was ever shipped on inland rvaterways of\nlndia since independence until November, 2018 and if not, the detail:s thereof;\n(c) the funds spent on development of industrial clusters and coastal communities\nso far;\n(d) ' whether intended targets in the aforesaid two fields have been met arnd if not, the\nreasons therefor;\n(e) whether any investigation has been made into the fake Sagarnala website\ncreated and if so, the details and the outcome thereof along wi'rh the action\ntaken thereon;\n(f) whether victims have been compensated by the Government and if so, the\ndetails thereof; and\n(S) the number of accidents about fishing boats hit by large vessels since 20'14 and\nthe number of fatalities, year-wise along with the measures taken to reduce the\nnumber of such accidents in future?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF SHIPPING\n(sHRt PON RADHAKRISHNAN)\n(a) Among the identified projects under Sagarmala programme, seven projects are\nfacing land acquisition issues. The details are annexed.\n(b) First containerized movement from Kolkata Port to Multimodal Terminal Varanasi\nthrough National Waterway (NW)-1 (Ganga- Bhagirathi - Hooghly river system) took\nplace in November,20l8.\n(c)&(d) Under the Port-led ind u stria lizatron and coastal community development\ncomponents of Sagarmala Programme, expenditure of Rs. 1,05,644 Cr has been\nincurred since the start of the programme tll2017-18.\nThese projects were planned for execution in a phased manner. A total of 506 projects\ncosting Rs.3.86 Lac Crore have been planned for award over a 4 year period from\n\n-z-\n2016 to 2020, out of which more than 50% projects or 267 projects costing Rs. 2.63 Lac\nCrore have already been awarded.\n266 projects costing Rs. 1 .8 Lac Crore were scheduled to be completed by 2020, out of\nwhich more than a third or 105 projects costing more than Rs. 16,500 Crore have\nalready been completed in just 2 years from the release of the National Perspective\nPlan.\n(e)&(f) Ministry of Shipping on 6 Sept 2A1B noticed that a fake\nwebsite www.sagarmala.org.in with a false advertisement about recruitment of Engineer\ntrainees and Diploma trainees was being used to dupe innocent job seekers by taking\nmoney in the name of Govt. job. The Ministry of Shipping immediately filed an FIR and\ngot the website taken down. On 1st October, 2018, it was again noticed that a new fake\nwebsite www.sagarproject.com with the same modus operandi as earlier was being\nused. Ministry of Shipping again referred the matter to Delhi Police and this matter was\nclubbed with the earlier FlR. As on date, Delhi Police is investigating the case.\n(g) The number of accidents about fishing boats hit by large vessels since 2014\nand the number of fatalities are presented in the table below:\nFollowing are the preventive measures taken to reduce number of incidents/accidents of\nfishing boat hit by large vessels,\n1. The Directorate General of Shipping has proposed the establishment of a Traffic\nSeparation Scheme (TSS) off the south-west coast of lndia to prevent such type\nof collision incidents. The initial and the subsequent revisions of the draft\nproposal for the establishment of TSS off the south-west coast of lndia has been\ncirculated to agencies of Central and State Government for their inputs.\n2. The Directorate General of Shipping has established ships' routing (such as\nTraffic Separation Schemes ITSS], Safety Fairways, etc.) in the past, so as to\nimprove safety of navigation in converging areas of traffic and in areas where the\ndensity of traffic is great or where freedom of movement of shipping in inhibited\nby restricted sea-room, the existence of obstructions to navigation, limited depths\nor unfavorable meteorological conditions. A ships routing helps in preventing or\nreducing the risk of pollution, loss of lives and other damage to the marine\nenvironment caused by ships colliding or grounding or anchoring in or near\nenvironmentally sensitive areas.\nYear Number of collision incidents\nreported between lndian merchant\nvessels and Fishing vessels\nNumber of fatalities\n2014 Nir Nit\n2015 01 Nit\n2016 01 Nit\n2017 05 3 dead, 4 missing\n2018 04 5 dead, '10 missing\n\n-3-\nAnnexure\nSr.\nNo. Name of the Project !mplementing\nAgency State\nLand to\nbe\nacquired\n1\nJNPT - 6 to B laning of NH-4B- SH-\n54 and Amra Marg NHAI Maharashtra 1.35 Ha\n2 New Line from Angul to Sukhinda lndian\nRailways Odisha 508\nAcres\n3 New Line from Haridaspur to\nParadip\nlnd ia n\nRailwavs Odisha 142.5 Ha\n4\nRail line Hospet-Hubli-Londa-\nTinaighat-Vasco da Gama "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |77", "t": "e-Learning Services", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \n     LOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 77 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \ne-Learning Services \n  \n77.   SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR: \n \n       Will the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware that e-lear ning services are being promoted in Government \nschools and colleges of the country;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether there is sufficient inve stment in providing e-learning faci lities, especially to schools and \ncolleges in backward areas of the country; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof?   \n  \n ANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n  (DR. SATYA PAL SINGH) \n \n(a) & (b) The key e-Learning Projects run by th e Ministry of Human Resource Development \n(MHRD) are as follows:  \n SWAYAM:- The ‘Study Webs of Active Learning fo r Young Aspiring Minds’ (SWAYAM) is an \nintegrated platform for online courses, using Information and Communication Technology (ICT) and \ncovering school (9th to 12th) to Post  Graduate Level.  It offers onlin e courses for students, teachers and \nteacher educators. It may be accessed on swayam.gov.i n.  National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS) is \npromoting education through e-learning methods by pr oviding courses on Mass ive Open Online Courses \n(MOOCs) on the portal. There are 44 courses of NI OS offered on SWAYAM platform – 14 at secondary \nlevel, 16 at senior secondary level, 4 vocational courses and 10 courses of Diploma in Elementary \nEducation (D.El.Ed.). NCERT has so far developed 22 courses for classes XI-XII in different subject \nareas. \n \n SWAYAM PRABHA:- A programme for utilization of sate llite communication technologies for \ntransmission of educational e-contents through 32 National Channels i.e. SWAYAM  PRABHA DTH-TV \nhas been launched. CIET-NCERT is the national coordinator for one DTH TV channel i.e., Kishore \nManch (#31) and has started feeding a 24x7 educational TV channel w.e.f. 09 .07.2018. Everyday four \nhour fresh slot is telecast and repeated 5 more times  in 24 hours to provide learning opportunities for the \nstake holders, as per thei r convenience.  Besides, NIOS is running 5 channels for teachers, for secondary \nand senior secondary levels and for sign language.  \n\n National Digital Library (NDL):  The National Digital Library of  India (NDL) is a project to \ndevelop a framework of virtual repository of learni ng resources with a single- window search facility. \nThere are more than 153 Lakhs digital books av ailable through the NDL. It may be accessed on \nndl.gov.in  \n \n ICT in Educational Curriculum for School System:  ICT curriculum for teachers and students has \nbeen developed by NCERT. Students’ curriculum was piloted in 588 Navodaya Vidyalayas for one year. \n805 MRPs/ KRPs of thirty states were oriented on roll -out of ICT curriculum for students and teachers in \nthe respective states. \n \n e-Pathshala: e-pathshala has been developed by NC ERT (National Council for Educational \nResearch and Training) for showcasing and disse minating all educational e-resources including \ntextbooks, audio, video, peri odicals and a variety of other print and non-print materials. So far, 3444 \naudios and videos, 698 e-books (e-pubs) and 504 flip books have been made ava ilable on the portal and \nmobile app. \n \n Shagun Portal – an Initiative to monitor the implementation of SSA:  A web portal called \nShaGun (from the words Shaala and Gunvatta) has a re pository of good practices, photographs, videos, \nstudies, newspaper articles etc. on elementary educa tion, State/UT wise. These are in the public domain. \nIts purpose is to showcase success stories and also to provide a platform for all stakeholders to learn from \neach other. This would also instill a positive competitive spirit among all the States and UTs.  \n \n National Repository of Open Educational Resources (NROER):  The National Repository of \nOpen Educational Resources (NROER) is an initiativ e to bring together all digital and digitisable \nresources across all stages of school education and teacher education. So far, 13635 files including \n401 collections, 2722 documents, 565 interactive, 1664 a udios, 2581 images and 6105 videos have been \nmade available over the portal.  States/ UTs are motivated to contri bute resources on NROER and create \nOERs for their own State/ UT.  \n \n KVS initiatives:- ICT Skills are imparted in all the Kendriya Vidyalayas to the students of classes \nIII to XII. 12011 e-Classrooms (9711 e-Classrooms es tablished and 2300 under process) have been \nestablished in Kendriya Vidyalaya s throughout the country for facil itating effective learning through \ndigital mode. Besides, 276 Digital Language Labs and 1137 Computer labs have been established in 276 \nKVs across the Country. Further, a pilot project e-Prajna has been started for providing tablets pre-loaded \nwith e-c"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |770", "t": "Demand and Supply", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF POWER \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.770 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \nDEMAND AND SUPPLY \n \n770. SHRI RAJESHBHAI CHUDASAMA: \n \n Will the Minister of POWER \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the status of power generation and  demand supply in the country \nand the details of the sources and their capacity in total power production \nin the country at present; and \n \n(b)  the sources from which carbon - free power would be generated in \nthe next ten years and the quantum of power  production fixed for these \nsources and the details of measures taken in this regard? \n \nA N S W E R \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR POWER  \nAND NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY  \n \n( SHRI  R. K. SINGH ) \n \n(a) :  The details of source wise power generation and their \ncapacity in total power production in the country during the current year \n2018-19 (upto December, 2018) and the status of demand and supply of \npower in the country are given at Annex. \n \n(b) :   Hydro, Nuclear and Renewable Energy (including Solar, Wind \nand Biomass) are main sources from which carbon free power would be \ngenerated in the next ten years.  \n \nGeneration of electricity is a delicensed activity and decision \nto set up any generating plants is based on a demand assessment by the \nconcerned generator. Hence no target has been fixed in the next ten \nyears. However, to promote clea n energy Government of India has fixed a \ntarget of 175 GW of renewable energy based generation capacity by 2022. \n \n...........2. \n\n \n \n- 2 - \n \n  The details of steps being taken by the Government to \npromote the production of renewable energy, inter alia, are as under: \n \ni. Fixed a target of 175 GW renewable energy based generation \ncapacity, out of which  100 GW would be solar power. \n \nii. Issued guidelines for procurement of solar and wind power through \ntariff based competitive bidding process; \n \niii. Declared Renewable Purchase Obligation (RPO) up to the year 2018 -\n19; \n \n \niv. Declare Renewable Generation Obligation on new coal/lignite based \nthermal plants; \n \nv. Notified National Offshore Wind Energy Policy; \nvi. Notified policy for Re-powering of Wind Power Projects; \nvii. Notified standards for deployment of solar photovoltaic \nsystems/devices; \nviii. Issued order for waiving inter State Transmission System charges \nand losses for inter -State sale of solar and wind based power \nprojects to be commissioned by December, 2019 and March 2019 \nrespectively. \n \n**************** \n  \n\n \n \n \nANNEX \n \nANNEX REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART  (a) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO.  770 TO BE ANSWERED IN THE LOK SABHA ON  \n07.02.2019.  \n*************** \n  \nSource wise generation and capacity in total power production in the \ncountry during the current year 2018-19 (Upto December, 2018) \nCategory Capacity (MW) Generation (MU) \nTHERMAL 2,23,027.34 8,05,433.52 \nNUCLEAR 6,780.00 28,457.54 \nHYDRO 45,399.22 1,16,041.57 * \nRES  74,081.66 97,923.70 \nGrand Total 3,49,288.22 10,47,856.33 \nNote: Generation from stations of 25 MW & above only \n* Includes Bhutan Import \n \n \n \nThe demand and supply of power in the country during April -\nDecember, 2018* \n \nEnergy (Million Unit) Peak (Mega Watt) \nEnergy \nRequirement \nEnergy \nSupplied \nEnergy \nNot \nSupplied \nPeak \nDemand \nPeak \nMet \nDemand \nnot Met \nMU MU MU % MW MW MW % \n971,490 965,589 5,901 0.6 177,022 175,528 1,494 0.8 \n*Provisional  \n \n************  \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |771", "t": "Details regarding HSS Yojana", "head": " \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.771 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \nDetails regarding HSS Yojana \n \n771. SHRI ASHOK SHANKARRAO CHAVAN:  \n \n Will the Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंरी   \nbe pleased to state; \n \n(a) whether the Government had launched Hathkargha Samvardhan Sahayata (HSS) Yojana for \nhandloom weavers; \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the aims and objectives thereto;  \n(c) the ratio of sharing of financial assistance between the Government and beneficiary; \n(d) the total financial assistance provided by t he Government under the HSS Yojana, till date, \nState/UT-wise;  \n(e) the number of handloom weavers benefited from the HSS, till date, State/UT-wise; and \n(f) the monitoring mechanism developed by the Government in this regard ? \n \nउत्तर \nANSWER \nवस्त्र राज्य मंरी  (श्री अजय टम्टा) \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR TEXTILES \n(SHRI AJAY TAMTA) \n \n \n(a) & (b) The Government of India, Minist ry of Textiles introduced the technology up -gradation \nscheme under National Handloom Development Programme (NHDP) and Comprehensive \nHandloom Cluster Development Scheme (CHCDS) in 2015 -16. The technology up -gradation \nscheme, with some modifications, was named as “Hathkargha Samvardhan Sahayata (HSS) \nYojana” in December 2016, for providing upgraded looms/accessories to  handloom weavers to \nimprove quality of fabric and enhance productivity . HSS is voluntary scheme  option, available for \nweavers for receiving support.  \n \n(c)     Under the Yojana, the Government of India bears 90% of the cost of looms/accessories & \nremaining 10% is borne by the beneficiary. \n \n(d)&(e)  A statement showing State -wise total financial assistance provided and the number of \nhandloom weavers benefited till date is at Annexure-I. \n \n(f)     The scheme  is monitored  at different level s by Government of India and State \nGovernment. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \nAnnexure-I \n \nStatement referred to in reply to parts (d) & (e ) of the Unstarred Question No. 771 dated \n07.02.2019 \n \nS. No. \n \nState Financial assistance provided \n(Rs. in lakh) \nNumber of handloom weavers \nbenefited \n 1 Kerala 100.41 868 \n 2 Tamil Nadu 819.37 9904 \n3 Telangana 65.61 220 \n4 Karnataka 45.84 236 \n5 Andhra Pradesh 448.53 386 \n6 Assam 784.96 821 \n7 Arunachal Pradesh 52.38 111 \n8 Meghalaya 27.97 129 \n9 West Bengal 383.68 142 \n10 Sikkim 13.77 20 \n11 Jharkhand 187.06 88 \n12 Tripura 59.09 1039 \n13 Manipur 14.66 121 \n14 Mizoram 118.48 1387 \n15 Bihar 160.36 0 \n16 Nagaland 268.62 40 \n17 Odisha 249.90 776 \n18  Uttar Pradesh 407.15 165 \n19 Uttrakhand 2.07 0 \n20 Jammu & Kashmir 123.46 188 \n21 Madhya Pradesh 45.69 47 \n22 Maharashtra 1.67 19 \n23 Chhattisgarh 83.17 235 \n24 Himachal Pradesh 34.88 0 \n25 Haryana 2.25 10 \n26 Rajasthan 5.64 41 \n  Total 4506.67 16993 \n  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |773", "t": "Physical Fitness Programme for Students", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 773 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \nPhysical Fitness Programme for Students \n \n773.  SHRI M.B. RAJESH: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to implement physical fitness \nprogrammes for the students across the country;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether any State Government is implementing specific programme \nfor increasing the level of physical fitness among the students; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n{COL. RAJYAVARDHAN RATHORE (RETD.)} \n \n(a) & (b) This Ministry is implementing Khelo India Scheme which has \ntwelve verticals. The Scheme, inter -alia, includes a vertical “Physical \nFitness of School going Children” . Under this vertical there is  provision \nfor providing a tool kit to each school to evaluate physical fitness of all \nschool goi ng children. Accordingly, steps have been taken to develop a \nmobile app for assessing the fitness level of the children between the age \ngroup of 5 to 18. This mobile app  is to be  provided to all schools in \nphased manner.  \n\n(c) & (d) „Sports‟ is a State subject and all the schemes implemented \nby States for development of sports  are not funded by this Ministry. \nTherefore, data in respect of schemes implemented by State \nGovernments including specific programme s for increasing the level o f \nphysical fitness among the students is not maintained in this Ministry.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |774", "t": "Construction of Roads in Rural Areas of Jharkhand", "head": " \nO.I.H. \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 774 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \n CONSTRUCTION OF ROADS IN RURAL AREAS OF JHARKHAND  \n \n774.  SHRI RAM TAHAL CHOUDHARY: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to take any ini tiative for construction of roads in the \nrural areas of the State of Jharkhand; \n  \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether the Government proposes to give financi al assistance in this regard;  \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and  \n(e) if not, the reasons therefor?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI RAM KRIPAL YADAV) \n \n(a)& (b): Rural Roads’ is a State subject and Pradh an Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana \n(PMGSY) is a one-time special intervention to provi de rural connectivity, by way of a single all-\nweather road, to the eligible unconnected habitatio ns in the core network with a population of \n500 persons and above (Census 2001) in plain areas.   In respect of  North Eastern States  (i.e. \nArunachal Pradesh, Assam, Manipur, Meghalaya, Mizor am, Nagaland, Sikkim and  Tripura) and \nHill States (i.e. Himachal Pradesh, Jammu & Kashmir  and Uttarakhand), the Desert Areas (as \nidentified in the Desert Development Programme), th e Tribal (Schedule V) areas and Selected \nTribal and Backward Districts (as identified by the  Ministry of Home Affairs (MHA) and the \nerstwhile Planning Commission), the objective is to  connect eligible unconnected habitations \nwith a population of 250 persons and above (Census 2001).  In the critical Left Wing Extremism \naffected blocks (as identified by MHA), additional relaxation has been given to connect \nhabitations with population 100 persons and above (2001 census). \nSince inception of the Scheme till 4 \nth  February, 2019, the State of Jharkhand has been sa nctioned \na total of 26,641.90 Km road length, out of which 2 0,885.88 Km road length has been completed \nand the remaining are in progress stage. \n \n (c)to (e): Rs. 6535.94 crore has been released to the State since inception till December, \n2018 for implementation of the PMGSY. As reported b y the State Government, an expenditure \nof Rs. 7,269.58 crore has been incurred till December, 2018.  \n*****  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|17|UNSTARRED |775", "t": "Electricity from Non-Conventional Sources", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENRGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 775 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2019 \n \nELECTRICITY FROM NON-CONVENTIONAL SOURCES \n \n775. SHRI PRATAPRAO JADHAV \n \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether  electricity production from non -conventional sources in the country especially Buldhana \nconstituency and other backward areas of Maharashtra State is under progress;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof as on date;  \n(c) the details of State-wise quantum of electricity production, State-wise;  \n(d) whether the Government have explored the possibility of electricity production from non -\nconventional sources especially in Buldhana constituency and other backward areas of Maharashtra \nState; and  \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER (I/C) \n(SHRI R. K. SINGH) \n \n(a) & (b) A total of 88.94 billion units (BU) of power has been generated from renewable sources in the \ncountry during the year 2018 -19 (up to November,  2018). A total of 9.81 BU of power has been \ngenerated from renewable sources in the state of Maharashtra during the year 2018 -19 (up to November, \n2018).      \n \nAs per Maharashtra Energy Development Agency (MEDA), one solar project  proposal in Buldhana \nconstituency has been forwarded to Maharashtra State Electricity Distribution Company Limited \n(MSEDCL) for obtaining technical feasibility for grid connectivity.   \n \n \n(c) The details of state -wise generation of electricity through renewable sources of energy during the \ncurrent year are given in Annexure.  \n \n(d) & (e) MEDA has installed six Wind monitoring stations for harnessing wind power in the   Buldhana \nconstituency. The details of wind monitoring stations installed in the Buldhana constituency are as \nfollows:- \nS. No. Site Taluka \n1 Dudha Buldhana \n2 Dagadwadi Deulgaon Raja \n3 Wazar Khamgaon \n4 Umapur Jalgaon-jamod \n5 Bhingara Jalgaon-jamod \n6 Harni Chikhli \n***** \n \n\nANNEXURE \nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (c) of Lok Sabha Un-starred question no. 775 to be answered \non 7/2/2019 regarding ‘Electricity from Non-conventional Sources’ \n \nThe details of state-wise generation of electricity through renewable sources of energy during the current \nyear:-  \n Generation  from  Various Renewable Energy Sources for the Year 2018 – 19 (Up to November 2018)                                                                                                                                                                              \n( All figures in MU ) \nSl. \nNo. State/Utility Wind Solar  Biomass Bagasse Small \nHydro Others Total \n1 Chandigarh 0.00 10.15 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00 10.15 \n2 Delhi 0.00 8.81 0.00 0.00 0.00 189.62 198.43 \n3 Haryana 0.00 44.77 129.90 75.58 167.51 0.00 417.76 \n4 HP 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00 1989.26 0.00 1989.26 \n5 J & K 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00 242.03 0.00 242.03 \n6 Punjab 0.00 1049.63 229.48 91.34 174.28 0.00 1544.73 \n7 Rajasthan 4964.30 2735.48 211.43 0.00 1.47 0.00 7912.68 \n8 Uttar Pradesh 0.00 766.31 65.37 1712.32 10